e-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=982767#post982767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it doesnt define noncombatant in the oath.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well then, it's either probably open season on allies of the enemy, or they're very careful to employ more stealth and trickery in missions against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:03:12-07:00","id":982914,"title":"","content":"oh I'd like some example uses and dice rolls for The provided abilitys<br /> <br /> Lets say that I'm a kinfolk working at pentex undercover. And I'm looking for some kind of Tax irregularity I can sic the Feds on.<br /> <br /> What attribute do I combine &quot;Burucracy&quot; with, and what difficulty<br /> <br /> Ditto with intuition what would you usualy combo it with and at what difficultys... if say I want to know if The guy im chatting with means to double cross me<br /> <br /> Oh another thing the Minor rite of Morning Song, it really redefines the setting I think by allowing QUITE A FEW Kinfolk to have access to Sense wyrm.<br /> <br /> I think its cool but game changing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 10-06-2016, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T21:56:12-07:00","id":983150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=982914#post982914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh I'd like some example uses and dice rolls for The provided abilitys<br /> <br /> Lets say that I'm a kinfolk working at pentex undercover. And I'm looking for some kind of Tax irregularity I can sic the Feds on.<br /> <br /> What attribute do I combine &quot;Burucracy&quot; with, and what difficulty<br /> <br /> Ditto with intuition what would you usualy combo it with and at what difficultys... if say I want to know if The guy im chatting with means to double cross me<br /> <br /> Oh another thing the Minor rite of Morning Song, it really redefines the setting I think by allowing QUITE A FEW Kinfolk to have access to Sense wyrm.<br /> <br /> I think its cool but game changing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Generally speaking the Bureaucracy roll would be contested I would probably use Wits + Bureaucracy to find the hidden money. If you were hiding the money it would depend on how you were hiding the money. <br /> <br /> Intuition I would go solely with Perception and that's if as a Storyteller didn't just roll it secretly. Intuition should be more about gut-feelings and less about dice.<br /> <br /> AS to the rest until I buy the book later today I have no comments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T22:57:01-07:00","id":983168,"title":"","content":"They have an entry for Tasers and Pepper Spray -- but no stats. Pepper Spray's stats are in Pentex: Subsidiaries, so no big deal, but I don't think Tasers have been statted anywhere before. Sort of an oversight, I think.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, however I'm quite impressed. I think this is a fairly robust improvement over Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T04:24:33-07:00","id":983246,"title":"","content":"As far as I understand this is not the final version of the book YET, so here goes<br /> <br /> 1A) I was delighted to find &quot;Media Sources of Inspiration&quot; in The V20 Ghouls Sourcebook, which surprisingly also included the Anime Masterpiece &quot;Puella Magi Madoka Magica&quot; as a source for &quot;devil's bargain stories&quot;<br /> Unfortunately, no such bibliography/filmoqgraphy/animeography exists in W20 Kinfolk; would this be rectified in the final PDF?<br /> 1B) if yes, might I recommend for the &quot;abusive home life in tribal cultures narratives&quot; stories the New Zealand Films &quot;Once Were Warriors&quot; and &quot;Whale Rider&quot;, both of which concern the disintegration of Maori Warrior Culture in the Modern Household.<br /> 1C) Not to mention the Kyoto Animation Series &quot;Clannad&quot; and its sequel &quot;Clannad After Story&quot;, which shows thoough you are tied down by birth families that may shatter your hopes and dreams, love still ultimately holds it together; not to mention the themes of &quot;the family you choose&quot;, &quot;heartbreak induced parental neglect&quot; and &quot;reconciliation with estranged children&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) Hopefully the various types of complications that Garou bring into a family that were elaborated in &quot;Unsung heroes: Kinfolk&quot; but largely unexplored in &quot;Kinfolk 20&quot; will be included too right? Of particular need to be explored is how a Garou child will feel about His Parents, whom he is although on paper &quot;superior&quot; to, but still somehow feels love and respect for? How DO you scold a child like that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T06:39:42-07:00","id":983283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=983168#post983168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have an entry for Tasers and Pepper Spray -- but no stats. Pepper Spray's stats are in Pentex: Subsidiaries, so no big deal, but I don't think Tasers have been statted anywhere before. Sort of an oversight, I think.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, however I'm quite impressed. I think this is a fairly robust improvement over Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 does have some taser rules but there is still some interpretation required. Like it doesn't say how long the charge lasts. If it's only one turn then you have to reload that's kind of lame. Technocratic taser bulleta discharge for 2 turns. If it's as long as the barbs are in them it's very strong bordering on OP since it requires a strength roll at diff 9 to dislodge yourself from an electrical source and each turn you take at least one health level of damage, even if it's bashing, stuns you for 1 turn per health level of damage dealt. Though tasers don't benefit from overages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T07:45:02-07:00","id":983313,"title":"","content":"I imagine that, when we look at the effect of tasers in real life, it would require a Stamina (difficulty 6, 4 if they are drunk) roll to avoid taking one bashing health level of damage and to avoid being incapacitated for one minute. If you botch your Stamina roll, you take one health level of lethal damage and, in addition to being incapacitated for an hour, you have to make a second Stamina roll (difficulty 6) to avoid a heart attack. I think that would accurately reflect the ineffectiveness of tasers (being tear gassed felt much worse) and the lethality of tasers (you will kill someone you repeatedly tase them twenty or thirty times).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T07:50:06-07:00","id":983318,"title":"","content":"So, I like this book a lot. It gives a sense of community among the kinfolk and gives a sense that they take -pride- in their position. However, they are also not just waiting at the garous' foot to serve, they do their own thing. Heck, they even have slurs for kin who are nothing but breedingstock.<br /> <br /> Generally, it is the right kind of uncomfortable, leaning very closely to the cults in Mummy the Curse. And that is a good thing, it should feel alien and cultish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T08:06:11-07:00","id":983328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=983318#post983318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I like this book a lot. It gives a sense of community among the kinfolk and gives a sense that they take -pride- in their position. However, they are also not just waiting at the garous' foot to serve, they do their own thing. Heck, they even have slurs for kin who are nothing but breedingstock.<br /> <br /> Generally, it is the right kind of uncomfortable, leaning very closely to the cults in Mummy the Curse. And that is a good thing, it should feel alien and cultish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this book have info about other breeds kinfolk? Specifically Mokole?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T08:34:13-07:00","id":983339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrostFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=983328#post983328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does this book have info about other breeds kinfolk? Specifically Mokole?</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone on the Onyx Path's <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/now-available-kinfolk-a-breed-apart/\" target=\"_blank\">main page for the release</a> mentioned something about the Mokole entry going full Chrono Trigger, like the old, pre-release version of the Mokole entry in W20 Changing Breeds, and presumably talking about Mokole ruling over humans before humans existed. I'm not able to confirm it just yet, but it holds a... kind of interest if it's true.<br /> <br /> On a tangential note regarding Mokole and the aforementioned pepper spray, it probably should have much of an effect on non-mammalian changers. The Ananasi, Corax, Mokole, Nagah, and Rokea should all more or less ignore its effects in their less human forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T08:44:14-07:00","id":983345,"title":"","content":"on equipment some attention to things invented in the last 20 years would have been appropiate.<br /> <br /> Id imagine that many kenning Kinfolk who have Dayjobs in town and only come out to the sept once or twice a month, probaly have wilderness survival guides and GPS on their smartphones<br /> <br /> anything else theyd have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T08:47:47-07:00","id":983347,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I need to read through Mokole stuff again in changing breeds but I thought it did describe them as guiding humanity after their fall from grace so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T10:22:10-07:00","id":983394,"title":"","content":"In terms of &quot;fractured/dysfunctional family dynasties that *hate* each other but are held together by blood/children/obligations&quot;, what other source materials would be good?<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head, I can think of <br /> <br /> &quot;Gone With the Wind&quot; (Rhett and Scarlet ONLY stayed together because of their daughter Bonnie, and resumed hating each other the day she died)<br /> <br /> &quot;What's Eating Gilbert Grape&quot; Starring Johnny Depp (painfully honest portrayal of great potential held back by ungrateful stupid kin in the archetypal &quot;dirt farming&quot; Fianna household<br /> <br /> Gilbert snapping at his autistic brother Arnie, (played by Leonardo DiCaprio), beating him and then storming off in remorse is the archetypal &quot;stress induced frenzy domestic violence&quot; scenario all too sadly common in Garou/Kin families)<br /> <br /> &quot;Interview With A Vampire&quot; (Lestat Embraced Claudia to bind Loius with parental love to a &quot;family&quot; he now hates, but must endure to protect his &quot;daughter&quot;)<br /> <br /> Any more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 10-07-2016, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T10:32:06-07:00","id":983398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrostFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=983347#post983347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. I need to read through Mokole stuff again in changing breeds but I thought it did describe them as guiding humanity after their fall from grace so to speak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm back from buying, downloading, and reading, and KABA has the most vicious reversal of the prior Mokole-kin relationship that there possibly could be, crossed over with presenting distorted Mnesis as the order of the day. While the prior presentation might have been too far to one side, the breedbook made a good case for Mokole not mistreating their kin, in the form of Mnesis passing those experiences of abuse on forever. Hence, giving them a ceremonial kind of position and title as the &quot;Eighth Sun&quot;, to keep noisome influences on the memory to a minimum. They have plenty to work with from the War of Rage, they want to avoid more.<br /> <br /> Rokea also have a bizarre writeup. Non-Betweeners are presented as being much more like Red Talons than immortals who intend to outlive humanity. Also, given the recent findings regarding Greenland sharks, the two to three years to maturity for maturity of shark-born and shark kin is... far shortcoming. To wit, the findings show that Greenland sharks live lifespans like early edition D&amp;D elves, taking what seems to be about a century and a half to reach sexual maturity, a state that they enjoy for the next two to three centuries, or perhaps more. While there are a lot of sharks that seem to take less time and be less long-lived, two or three years is still way too few. There's also the additional problem of the fact that Rokea technically don't have Kinfolk; all Rokea-on-shark matings are treated the same way, unless someone is going to writeup material to contradict the breedbook, and it seems that no one actually has.<br /> <br /> Let's also talk about how much word count is wasted on the discussion of the term &quot;gene&quot;. Since Revised, it was a case of &quot;there is none, no, end of story&quot; and then we'd get on with things, unrestrained from the painfully-like-Liquid Snake issues of prior editions. But For KABA, there's at least a half page about it trying to link being Garou to a single inheritable factor, whatever it might be. It does admit that no one can find it, or hasn't found it yet. It's also irritating for mentioning Progenitors as trying to get in on the action, because quite frankly, that setting and this one don't mix at all without everything blowing up.<br /> <br /> So, no, page 8, I don't accept what you're trying to sell me about most modern Garou referring to their ineffable state as being caused by a gene, even if it's in scare quotes. The ones who don't know much about it probably reject it as a term not becoming of spirit, and those that do probably reject it on the basis that there's nothing that they can isolate. Maybe next you'd like to convince me that someone is trying to figure out where their Crinos mass goes, using only typical instruments for gravity anomalies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T11:25:27-07:00","id":983421,"title":"","content":"I really like the art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T13:32:33-07:00","id":983498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=983313#post983313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that, when we look at the effect of tasers in real life, it would require a Stamina (difficulty 6, 4 if they are drunk) roll to avoid taking one bashing health level of damage and to avoid being incapacitated for one minute. If you botch your Stamina roll, you take one health level of lethal damage and, in addition to being incapacitated for an hour, you have to make a second Stamina roll (difficulty 6) to avoid a heart attack. I think that would accurately reflect the ineffectiveness of tasers (being tear gassed felt much worse) and the lethality of tasers (you will kill someone you repeatedly tase them twenty or thirty times).</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were writing the rules for Tasers (as someone who has been hit with one -- in training), I'd do it this way (assuming an &quot;Air-Taser&quot;): Dex + Firearms attack roll, just like a handgun. If the roll succeeds, additional successes add to damage as normal (prongs hit over a wider area -- which worsens the effect), with a base rating of 6 Bashing (I'd also make &quot;Animal-Tasers&quot; -- which <i>do</i> exist, although I don't believe Taser International isn't marketing them anymore -- available with a code of 8 Bashing). Since it's Bashing, soak<i> is </i>possible, but with a twist: In <i>addition</i> to the basic Bashing damage, for the turn that the character is hit, any <i>boxes</i> of Bashing damage that he incurs in that round after soak, is tacked onto his Dex penalty (So if he takes 6 Bashing and soaks one, for that round he suffers a -7 Dex penalty -- -2 for the basic wound penalty and -5 for the number of boxes he didn't soak). If the target reaches Incapacitated, in addition to any overflow boxes (which become Lethal as normal), he has to roll Stamina -- a botch by a PC or important NPC results in a heart attack, with an additional box of Lethal each turn until somebody does an Wits + Medicine roll or otherwise heals him. A simple failure for an average NPC results in a heart attack.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For the turn that he get hit with the Taser, if the Dex penalty exceeds the character's total Dexterity (including form modifiers), the character is effectively immobilized and loses all actions that turn. A successful Rage roll (one net success) will negate this effect. Werewolves getting hit with a Taser must immediately check for Frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 10-07-2016, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T14:52:05-07:00","id":983546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=983398#post983398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I'm back from buying, downloading, and reading, and KABA has the most vicious reversal of the prior Mokole-kin relationship that there possibly could be, crossed over with presenting distorted Mnesis as the order of the day. While the prior presentation might have been too far to one side, the breedbook made a good case for Mokole not mistreating their kin, in the form of Mnesis passing those experiences of abuse on forever. Hence, giving them a ceremonial kind of position and title as the &quot;Eighth Sun&quot;, to keep noisome influences on the memory to a minimum. They have plenty to work with from the War of Rage, they want to avoid more.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So I can't get the pdf till next Friday due to budgets...but am I understanding your post that the new Kinfolk book did a 180 from how the Mokole breed book covered kin relations? I was always fan of the concept of the 8th sun.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T15:27:01-07:00","id":983563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=983546#post983546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So I can't get the pdf till next Friday due to budgets...but am I understanding your post that the new Kinfolk book did a 180 from how the Mokole breed book covered kin relations? I was always fan of the concept of the 8th sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I'm just going to disregard this book's approach to Mokole Kin, since it clashes with almost everything else, including other W20 material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7621-threadwrought","name":"Threadwrought","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T15:41:31-07:00","id":983571,"title":"","content":"That's a huge disappointment that I'll probably just ignore. The mokole drew me in because I've always been a big herp fanboy, but the culture that several of the source books laied out I found interesting. The fact they were so close with their kin and had a huge sense of family was one of the major draws for me. I thought it was different to have reptilian critters depicted in such a way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T17:26:46-07:00","id":983625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=983398#post983398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I'm back from buying, downloading, and reading, and KABA has the most vicious reversal of the prior Mokole-kin relationship that there possibly could be, crossed over with presenting distorted Mnesis as the order of the day. While the prior presentation might have been too far to one side, the breedbook made a good case for Mokole not mistreating their kin, in the form of Mnesis passing those experiences of abuse on forever. Hence, giving them a ceremonial kind of position and title as the &quot;Eighth Sun&quot;, to keep noisome influences on the memory to a minimum. They have plenty to work with from the War of Rage, they want to avoid more.<br /> <br /> Rokea also have a bizarre writeup. Non-Betweeners are presented as being much more like Red Talons than immortals who intend to outlive humanity. Also, given the recent findings regarding Greenland sharks, the two to three years to maturity for maturity of shark-born and shark kin is... far shortcoming. To wit, the findings show that Greenland sharks live lifespans like early edition D&amp;D elves, taking what seems to be about a century and a half to reach sexual maturity, a state that they enjoy for the next two to three centuries, or perhaps more. While there are a lot of sharks that seem to take less time and be less long-lived, two or three years is still way too few. There's also the additional problem of the fact that Rokea technically don't have Kinfolk; all Rokea-on-shark matings are treated the same way, unless someone is going to writeup material to contradict the breedbook, and it seems that no one actually has.<br /> <br /> Let's also talk about how much word count is wasted on the discussion of the term &quot;gene&quot;. Since Revised, it was a case of &quot;there is none, no, end of story&quot; and then we'd get on with things, unrestrained from the painfully-like-Liquid Snake issues of prior editions. But For KABA, there's at least a half page about it trying to link being Garou to a single inheritable factor, whatever it might be. It does admit that no one can find it, or hasn't found it yet. It's also irritating for mentioning Progenitors as trying to get in on the action, because quite frankly, that setting and this one don't mix at all without everything blowing up.<br /> <br /> So, no, page 8, I don't accept what you're trying to sell me about most modern Garou referring to their ineffable state as being caused by a gene, even if it's in scare quotes. The ones who don't know much about it probably reject it as a term not becoming of spirit, and those that do probably reject it on the basis that there's nothing that they can isolate. Maybe next you'd like to convince me that someone is trying to figure out where their Crinos mass goes, using only typical instruments for gravity anomalies?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd like more info on this....seems to run counter to most OP W20 information. Parawolf changes/inclusions? or just not checked properly?<br /> <br /> <br /> Still the pdf is not the final version, now is the time for them to fix it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T17:34:49-07:00","id":983632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=983625#post983625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd like more info on this....seems to run counter to most OP W20 information. Parawolf changes/inclusions? or just not checked properly?<br /> <br /> <br /> Still the pdf is not the final version, now is the time for them to fix it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope they do. It really feels like whoever wrote this portion just skimmed the Mokole entry in the W20 sourcebook or Changing Breeds and took all the wrong things from it. It was seriously them taking what had been stated to be a rare/occasional aberration and corrupted piece -some- of the Mokole's Mnesis in all previous W20 and WtA material, and treating it as the rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7621-threadwrought","name":"Threadwrought","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T17:41:46-07:00","id":983636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=983571#post983571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a huge disappointment that I'll probably just ignore. The mokole drew me in because I've always been a big herp fanboy, but the culture that several of the source books laied out I found interesting. The fact they were so close with their kin and had a huge sense of family was one of the major draws for me. I thought it was different to have reptilian critters depicted in such a way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thankfully, the Zhong Lung's tune didn't change on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T17:43:06-07:00","id":983638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Threadwrought</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=983632#post983632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really hope they do. It really feels like whoever wrote this portion just skimmed the Mokole entry in the W20 sourcebook or Changing Breeds and took all the wrong things from it. It was seriously them taking what had been stated to be a rare/occasional aberration and corrupted piece -some- of the Mokole's Mnesis in all previous W20 and WtA material, and treating it as the rule.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> think there is some way to get this communicated so the pdf may get some alterations in that 1 aspect? I mean if it runs counter to already produced W20 stuff....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T17:44:01-07:00","id":983640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=983636#post983636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thankfully, the Zhong Lung's tune didn't change on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>*sigh* I've never been huge on that Stream....reading it growing up it always felt like there was an over emphasis on that Stream, followed by the Gumagan, so it always bugged me. I'm not thrilled that the largest stream apparently will lose this whole concept of the importance of Kin and the 8th sun, I really liked that part of pan-mokole culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 10-07-2016, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T18:27:43-07:00","id":983661,"title":"","content":"oh on Garou Rites kinfolk can learn any thoughts on these 3<br /> <br /> <br /> The rite of cleansing, it would make Wyrm taint far more vulnerable to eradication<br /> <br /> The Rite of Binding.<br /> <br /> Would allow Kin to work as &quot;Support Staff&quot; keeping the Natioin well stocked with Talens<br /> <br /> The Questing Stone.<br /> <br /> Wheither your a Bounty Hunter, police officer or social worker, it would be a great asset in your mundane life.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: MAY I HAVE YOUR ATTENTION.<br /> <br /> I have found an error in the Renown chart, at least I think its an error.<br /> <br /> lose 1 Wisdom for siring or bearing Garou offspring?<br /> <br /> WTF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 10-07-2016, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T01:20:56-07:00","id":983821,"title":"","content":"In lieu of a proper errata thread, I'll go ahead and mention here that the section on Numina references an experience/freebie point cost chart that doesn't exist. (It specifically refers to a &quot;following chart&quot;)<br /> <br /> <i>Edit: Upon further examination, I correct myself. The freebie point chart exists, but nowhere near the Numina section. It's on page 58, as part of a sidebar that also implies, without context, that a character can only purchase two Numina and has asterisks with no connected footnotes. The experience point chart is still nowhere to be found.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":171,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","user":"MythicFox","date":".  There was some unhelpful, unfair, and somewhat inappropriate wording in my initial post/edit. I apologize for the now-removed remark. 10-08-2016, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T20:40:36-07:00","id":984206,"title":"","content":"Another &quot;Screwed Up Family that still loves each other&quot; Film to add to the (hopeful) filmography for &quot;Kinfolk W20&quot;<br /> <br /> Little Miss Sunshine (2006)<br /> <br /> A family that can barely spend three minutes without yelling at each other takes their youngest daughter, the only remotely happy and sane individual, on a Cross-Continent-Road-Trip to a Little-Miss-Beauty Pagent.<br /> <br /> Pay close attention to the rude-and-perverted Grandfather and the Resentful Introverted Teenage-Goth Son: the former as inspiration for an ex-Garou who has &quot;lost the wolf&quot; but still thinks that the rules of &quot;polite-society&quot; no longer applies to him, and the latter as another fine example of &quot;young kinfolk with potential and a future held back by a stupid and selfish Garou/Kin&quot;<br /> <br /> They often *do* almost tear each other to pieces (minus the Crinos-Forms, of course), but are in the end held together by their collective love for their little girl, whom they are determined to keep innocent and happy in spite of their anger and bitterness towards each-other. (Much like how Garou ultimately still do love their kin, and vice versa) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 10-08-2016, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T22:22:31-07:00","id":984254,"title":"","content":"While I've been enjoying some parts of the book I've been looking at, I must make a specific comment: Conjuration is just awful. Requiring separate rituals for all types of items you could prepare and REQUIRING you to ritually prepare any object you want to manipulate? It makes it just about useless except for parlor tricks and the occasional weapon conjuring when your hands are kept from your pockets (or other 10 foot away location). Maybe levitating a friend at the fifth dot, but who would spill enough xp into it to get to that level anyway?<br /> <br /> Granted, it's easy enough to houserule away the requirement for ritual preparation, instead just making that remove wp costs like in Sorc revised, but still, it's a terrible default.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T23:03:28-07:00","id":984269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=982914#post982914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh I'd like some example uses and dice rolls for The provided abilitys<br /> <br /> Lets say that I'm a kinfolk working at pentex undercover. And I'm looking for some kind of Tax irregularity I can sic the Feds on.<br /> <br /> What attribute do I combine &quot;Burucracy&quot; with, and what difficulty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually i would say tax law stuff would come under a Law skill, not bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=983313#post983313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that, when we look at the effect of tasers in real life, it would require a Stamina (difficulty 6, 4 if they are drunk) roll to avoid taking one bashing health level of damage and to avoid being incapacitated for one minute. If you botch your Stamina roll, you take one health level of lethal damage and, in addition to being incapacitated for an hour, you have to make a second Stamina roll (difficulty 6) to avoid a heart attack. I think that would accurately reflect the ineffectiveness of tasers (being tear gassed felt much worse) and the lethality of tasers (you will kill someone you repeatedly tase them twenty or thirty times).</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see dropping the diff if on PSP or the like for resisting a taser, but not just from being drunk. If anything i would also rise up the base diff, to 7 at least..<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T01:39:52-07:00","id":984312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=984269#post984269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could see dropping the diff if on PSP or the like for resisting a taser, but not just from being drunk. If anything i would also rise up the base diff, to 7 at least..<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would include something about how as soon as the Taser is off, you're basically back to normal. You can literally just pop right back up like nothing happened (aside from walking sort of funny for a couple of seconds).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T06:57:03-07:00","id":984375,"title":"","content":"In real life, alcohol seems to change the conductivity enough to allow really drunk people to resist tasers more effectively. Stimulants, however, make them more lethal, with drugs like PCP making a heart attack more likely (the botch requirement would become a failure requirement). At least that is what I have seen in the criminal justice literature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T07:11:02-07:00","id":984380,"title":"","content":"Is finding an Aldich Ames, like financial irregularity, a buerucracy matter then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T08:03:24-07:00","id":984403,"title":"","content":"Garous may be strongest creatures in WoD but kinkfolk may be wiser and that is important. To be the leader you don't need to be the boss. A veteran kinfolk with good ideas and advices can help more than a stupy rookie Garou. <br /> <br /> I love to destroy the cannon bakcground and mixing ideas from different franchises. One of my ideas is a variation of skin darcers tribe. They would kinfolk who hunt another kinfolk and with a special ritual they become demi-fera, (for gameplay effects like Banes, but with a totally different background, closer to pure tribes from &quot;Werewolf: the forsaken&quot;).<br /> <br /> Another idea is kinkfolk can travel and live in &quot;uchronies&quot;, like spirit realms, demiplanes, or parallel earths, where Nature prevails but there are other menaces like a zombie-apocalipse, prehistoric ice age, or invanders from altenate timelines. These kinkfolks are prey and predators, with their own reasons to fear the &quot;other wolves&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T08:35:53-07:00","id":984427,"title":"","content":"Am I the only person who thinks Spirit chasing could do with some more clarifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcod