r=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T17:08:45-07:00","id":984659,"title":"","content":"on 19 it came up in my &quot;socially conservative Ragabash&quot; thread that wound up descending into some people bashing Feminism sadly, but one of the ways some people said to present a conservative Ragabash is to question NEW rules as much as the old ones, like<br /> <br /> &quot;Kinfolk are equal to the garou&quot; then they should hold equal responsiblety in a fight.<br /> <br /> &quot;Metis dont deserve derision&quot; even though Gaia cursed them? What else do you think shes doing wrong?<br /> <br /> was one or two other points but you get the idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T21:32:28-07:00","id":985264,"title":"","content":"Oh curious<br /> <br /> if a Kinfolk using the Healing or Empathic healing Numina to cure a worthy non kinfolk human, of a serious disease, how could the veil withstand it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T07:03:50-07:00","id":985390,"title":"","content":"It mentions that some Shadow Lord Kin learn soul stealing to gain power in their tribe.<br /> <br /> Separately from references from Rebel kin<br /> <br /> think the Shadow lords grudgingly tolerate such studies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:58:06-07:00","id":985570,"title":"","content":"I really don't like the changes to the Setting W20 is rolling out.<br /> Rites for Kin.<br /> The 'Baptism of Fire' now for Kin and Garou, since on can't tell the difference anymore as of W20.<br /> <br /> I have been asking for the tribes believes for an afterlife or death myths since before W20, so it's nice that it has a paragraph in this book, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:01:37-07:00","id":985575,"title":"","content":"I understand your discomfort with any retcons Heinrich, but given how contradictary a lot of prior material is on the issue, I prefer it this way.<br /> <br /> <br /> It makes it so a garou or kinfolk can be raised &quot;In the know&quot; without killing any potential drama.<br /> <br /> I was a little disappointed at Kin having rites, but I' had complained myself that Kinfolk were too weak against ghouls, so what did I want them to do?<br /> <br /> Rite of the Morning Song, greatly enhances the number of kin with Sense Wyrm, thus making the Garou much more aware of wyrmish activity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 10-11-2016, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T18:18:48-07:00","id":985838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=985570#post985570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't like the changes to the Setting W20 is rolling out.<br /> Rites for Kin.<br /> The 'Baptism of Fire' now for Kin and Garou, since on can't tell the difference anymore as of W20.</div> </div> </div> </div>I often wonder at how Garou and Fera - particularly Mokole - can get along like that. Marry the wrong kin who's a late changer, and you break the litany/the duties, and the latter breakage is extremely severe, since the ghost reptile baby will haunt its parents and then everyone else for <i>forever</i>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T18:22:50-07:00","id":985843,"title":"","content":"Im sure that Amongs the garou the Renown loss will be waived, with a shake of the head, and amongst the Well heeled tribes (fangs, fianna, shadow lords glass walkers) Lawyers who answer to the tribe will get to work, immediately annulling the marriage, or they might have to go through an uncontested divorce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T18:46:58-07:00","id":985862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=985838#post985838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I often wonder at how Garou and Fera - particularly Mokole - can get along like that. Marry the wrong kin who's a late changer, and you break the litany/the duties, and the latter breakage is extremely severe, since the ghost reptile baby will haunt its parents and then everyone else for <i>forever</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the Gumagan eat their Metis babies so they don't haunt them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T20:51:07-07:00","id":985924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrostFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=985862#post985862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the Gumagan eat their Metis babies so they don't haunt them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one Stream out of four. Though really, I'm not sure why the others wouldn't, given the consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T02:23:27-07:00","id":986012,"title":"","content":"Granted, the editors of the past havn't done a grat job to keep the setting streamlines, but this changes don't make things clearer but blatantly things again.<br /> <br /> And it isn't something that changed in the Setting, but something that in the Setting is presented as having been different from what it was in the last editions since forever. So, it's not that Kin recently started to work rites and now have found the ability to do so, but that it has been that way all the time. That makes a lot of other material invalid.<br /> <br /> If I go to a convention, I have to start to describe character actions as &quot;My character would do &lt;insert action&gt;, because I believe that this would work within the Setting, since &lt;fact a&gt; and &lt;fact b&gt; support the assumption. I know that &lt;source c&gt; contradicts this claim seemingly, but what is described there is in my opinion a special case, not applicable to the situation. As for &lt;source d&gt;, well, that is a in-character narration within the book with exaggeration and therefore not a viable argument on the matter. That said, I haven't read &lt;source e&gt; of the W20 gameline yet, altough it probably deals with the matter, too.&quot;<br /> <br /> And that is just annoying.<br /> As a player I would have loved a encyclopedic book for WtA like V20 was for V20.<br /> <br /> All the re-working of the 2nd and revised era books with changes to the Setting and ret-conning really is no fan service.<br /> I feel we are back to a kind of ruling by whom ever is in charge of a certain book or game line and farther away from an open development then ever.<br /> For a game that kind of promotes collaborative storytelling this sucks. For I don't feel much collaboration going on, when the Setting, as the story foundation, is changed seemingly randomly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T15:06:54-07:00","id":986417,"title":"","content":"You know... I don't really see how the &quot;new&quot; Rites change anything. It already says that most of the Rites for Kin (the lower-level ones at any rate) have no actual effect. Most of the ones that <i>do</i> have an effect need Garou participants. The few exceptions sort of assume that a spirit is pleased by the attention the Kin is paying them via the Rite and decides to empower the Rite. There's nothing that says that if the spirit doesn't want to empower the Rite, it has to. The only thing that specifies that a spirit has to empower a Rite and has no choice in the matter is in the main rulebook, which specifically states that only Garou can perform a Rite and <i>expect</i> it to work. I haven't seen anything in Kinfolk: a Breed Apart that contradicts that.<br /> <br /> I think you don't like this because you've gotten so wrapped up in the idea that spirits <i>do not, will not, cannot </i>empower Rites for <i>anyone</i> other than a Garou, <i>ever</i>, that this is violating your worldview of WoD. As long as the storyteller is competent, and approaches it intelligently this shouldn't be an issue. And besides, if you're the storyteller, you get to say &quot;yeah, but not in my game&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T15:18:22-07:00","id":986427,"title":"","content":"what about the &quot;Minor&quot; rite of the morning song, which is world changing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T16:05:21-07:00","id":986449,"title":"","content":"I don't have the book, but am considering picking it up. Some questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Other posts on this thread imply that Kinfolk Rites are mostly social in nature, with a handful that have supernatural power at the pleasure of the empowering spirit; that seems fine to me. But what about Kinfolk Gifts?<br /> 2. Numina. I won't be surprised to learn that there are Psychic Phenomena in the book, since the Werewolf lines have traditionally been where mortal psychic powers have been featured. I'm curious which ones have been included. Sorcerous Paths are a bit more of a surprise, and I'm curious which ones made the cut. In particular, I'm wondering if any of the ones introduced in the Dreamspeakers Revised Tradition Book made it into KABA. (If it were me, I'd probably include the Summoning/Binding/Warding Path, the <b>Dreamspeakers</b> Paths, and a fetish-making variant of the item-making Path.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-12-2016, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T16:28:49-07:00","id":986461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=986427#post986427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what about the &quot;Minor&quot; rite of the morning song, which is world changing.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is that &quot;world changing&quot;? Where has it ever been said that spirits who are pleased by a non-Garou performing a Rite somehow <i>cannot</i> empower the Rite? Moreover, where does it say that if the spirits are <i>not</i> pleased by a Kin's performance of the Rite (or the spirits just don't want to), that they <i>have to </i>empower the Rite? The main rulebook states emphatically that the Great Spirit Pact applies to the shapechangers and only to them. Everything else is gravy. What stops the storyteller from deciding that the Kin having the easy ability to sense that an antagonist is a Wyrm-tainted Black Spiral Dancer, disrupts the story, and simply says that &quot;yeah, you perform the Rite flawlessly and you think you did a good job, but you can instantly tell that the spirits aren't listening today&quot;?<br /> <br /> \u200bWe know that the Ritual of Sacred Rebirth <i>can</i> be enacted by Kinfolk. So why not others? I hate to revive this flame-war, but I'm genuinely not getting what the issue is here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 10-12-2016, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T16:40:25-07:00","id":986465,"title":"","content":"Whats world changing is putting the gift &quot;Sense Wyrm&quot; in the hands of a good percentage of kenning kinfolks hands, thus allowing a Sept to be much more aware when a business, or home is wyrm tainted.<br /> <br /> oh, ideas how to make a Fetch Hawk, a viable encounter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T03:40:16-07:00","id":986661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=986417#post986417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you don't like this because you've gotten so wrapped up in the idea that spirits <i>do not, will not, cannot </i>empower Rites for <i>anyone</i> other than a Garou, <i>ever</i>, that this is violating your worldview of WoD. As long as the storyteller is competent, and approaches it intelligently this shouldn't be an issue. And besides, if you're the storyteller, you get to say &quot;yeah, but not in my game&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like it, because it was stated before that a kin person could learn or teach a Rite but not enact it. It was a hard rule, with an exception. Not to retcon, that there have been, all along, ways to do Rites, if garou are participation, or maybe even without - for normal kinfolk is a Retcon and I hate those.<br /> For me Retcons and Reboots destroyed Ultimate Marvel and the DC Universe - I hate it happening in Werewolf, too.<br /> <br /> We are all adults here. It would be common decency to have a sidebar and give an honest out-of-character statement to world changes. Something like:<br /> &quot;In early Werewolf sidestepping was limited to places where reflecting or shiny surfaces were available. Different authors weren't always on the same page on how the process works, though. In <i>Valkenburg Foundation</i> the surface was in the umbra, while in <i>Rite of Passage</i> a blinking earring would have allowed ambushing an inexperienced Wendigo pack's campsite by sidestepping out of the Umbra right between them. By revised edition it was possible for garou to attempt to sidestep anywhere, the reflecting surface merely reducing difficulty by one. In our opinion, this made the Penumbra too easy to reach and reduced the gravitas of the question on which side of the Gauntlet a character was. That's why for W20 we changed the system again, stating that it is normal to use stationary mirrors or reflecting surfaces as means to cross the Gauntlet. Portable mirrors also work, but at increased difficulty. Sidestepping without those means is not permitted.<br /> You can either assume the world always worked like presented here, or regard this change as something that happened in the last few years. You can also play W20 using the sidestepping rules from revised edition, although this might require further adjusting in regards to gifts etc.<br /> If you allow gifts from previous editions, we suggest to raise the Stargazer cliath gift <i>Inner Light</i>, that allows to sidestepp without a mirror, to Fostern Rank and possibly make it available to all Theurges, if you find the W20 rules to restricting, but don't want to use the revised rules, either.&quot;<br /> <br /> Something like that - comment from game designer to player/storyteller on what a given mechanic is about and how it came to be and how it is changed from other editions of the game would make the whole W20 stuff much more accessible.<br /> Also, the whole &quot;Can't detect pre-change garou anymore, and never could&quot;-aspect would be a lot more thought through if someone had bothered to explain, why the change felt necessary for the development team, how it was handled before, how one could ease the transition and so on...<br /> <br /> So, no, it is not that I don't like the Rites for Kin people because I am stuck in my metaphysical belief of how spirits should handle Rites in this fictional Setting. I would have allowed Kin rites anyhow, if they were the tools (Foci) to perform True Magic (which is canon) or Hedge Magic (which is kind of canon, because Sorcerers need a craft/tradition like basis for their sorcery and while not explicitly listed garou shamanism falls within the scope of what players/ST are encouraged to design for their characters).<br /> The way the book handles Rites, and gitfts for that matter, is just kind of unsatifactory for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 10-13-2016, 06:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T07:16:37-07:00","id":986744,"title":"","content":"Isn't the whole point of the 20th anniversary stuff that it's a mostly continuity-free sandbox? You can't retcon without con to ret.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T08:28:27-07:00","id":986773,"title":"","content":"the book has both Healing and Empathic Healing<br /> <br /> Not sure why to take empathic healing when you can take healing, unless your <br /> <br /> and Divination, a slightly different form then the one from Hunters Hunted II<br /> <br /> Man, im going to use this in my game.<br /> <br /> Conjuration is in the PDF but, doesnt look worthwhile to me<br /> <br /> Herbalism/Brewing. Basicly alchemy &quot;sanitized&quot; for the Garous approval.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T13:47:21-07:00","id":986932,"title":"","content":"I get retconning to be annoying, and I agree with you on the stepping sideways issue (to a degree), but...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=986661#post986661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like it, because it was stated before that a kin person could learn or teach a Rite but not enact it. It was a hard rule...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah -- according to you. You've been banging the drum pretty hard that Kin can't do Rites for a long time, and anytime someone (like me, for instance) brings up evidence that seems to indicate that that's not <i>exactly</i> how it works, you ignore it and just keep insisting that you're right. Now the canon <i>specifically</i> states that it works more along the lines of &quot;yeah, but it's not a hard and fast rule and there are exceptions -- and here's a few of them...&quot;. Isn't it just <i>possible</i> that your interpretation wasn't entirely spot-on? Because this &quot;new&quot; take is how I've always read it from the very beginning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T13:50:24-07:00","id":986934,"title":"","content":"Id have to agree with him, that it is basicly a retcon.<br /> <br /> But I've complained more then once, about Kinfolk being overly weak against ghouls, this is a valid way to fix it.<br /> <br /> Have to wonder, can kinfolk enact the rite of binding its only a level 2 rite.<br /> <br /> or cleansing.<br /> <br /> I could see a kinfolk with gnosis, put to work in one of those tasks, to spare garou attention for worthier tasks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T14:11:09-07:00","id":986943,"title":"","content":"Morning Song is very similar to Greet the Sun. It's a Rite in which the participant literally sings the praises of a spirit (in this case Helios). I don't think that a Solar-Gaffling nearby deciding to reward the Kinfolk for the song of praise is too out-there. Kin being able to use Rites in the same way that the Garou do (any Rite just whenever they need them) <i>does</i> fundamentally alter the relationship. I'm not in favor of that.<br /> <br /> Now, most Rites could (theoretically) be enacted by a Kin, but it would be dependent upon the spirit in question. If it's like the Garou, where some werewolf does a Rite to cleanse Wyrm-Taint, and any spirit floating along is required to enact it (as opposed to responding to a direct appeal of praise directed at that very spirit), I don't see that happening. The Great Spirit Pact should still apply. If the Rite is going to work for a Kinfolk, there should be a <i>reason</i> -- and that reason should be that the spirit <i>wants to </i>(for whatever justification).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 10-13-2016, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T16:06:27-07:00","id":986993,"title":"","content":"I cant find the Experience cost that Kinfolk pay per Rite they learn<br /> <br /> wheres it listed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T19:32:44-07:00","id":987061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=986943#post986943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Morning Song is very similar to Greet the Sun. It's a Rite in which the participant literally sings the praises of a spirit (in this case Helios). I don't think that a Solar-Gaffling nearby deciding to reward the Kinfolk for the song of praise is too out-there. Kin being able to use Rites in the same way that the Garou do (any Rite just whenever they need them) <i>does</i> fundamentally alter the relationship. I'm not in favor of that.<br /> <br /> Now, most Rites could (theoretically) be enacted by a Kin, but it would be dependent upon the spirit in question. If it's like the Garou, where some werewolf does a Rite to cleanse Wyrm-Taint, and any spirit floating along is required to enact it (as opposed to responding to a direct appeal of praise directed at that very spirit), I don't see that happening. The Great Spirit Pact should still apply. If the Rite is going to work for a Kinfolk, there should be a <i>reason</i> -- and that reason should be that the spirit <i>wants to </i>(for whatever justification).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Morning song is arguably a game changer, yet is listed as a &quot;minor&quot; rite, I think it should be AT LEAST level 2.<br /> <br /> or is it just the repetetive practice that gave it this classification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"im