d and fast XP cost per rite, somewhere.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><i>During Character Creation</i>, Rites cost 1 Background Dot per level of Rituals, with Minor Rites costing half.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T14:37:05-07:00","id":987941,"title":"","content":"sighs your probaly right.<br /> <br /> oh<br /> <br /> A question can anyone think of a use for &quot;Biting Bullet&quot; other then assasination, with or without infiltration.<br /> <br /> oh the Garou Favor Background, it doesnt really seem appropiate for continual indebtedness if a Kin is hosting a Garou or pack in the long term.<br /> <br /> Is it safe to say in most cases that would be a situation with both advantages and disadvantages<br /> <br /> anyone who breaks into your house will likely regret it very soon.<br /> <br /> but you have to furnish them with cash food possibly clothes.at best<br /> <br /> and put up with tantrums, possibly abuse at worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 10-15-2016, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T02:18:29-07:00","id":988747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=986744#post986744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't the whole point of the 20th anniversary stuff that it's a mostly continuity-free sandbox? You can't retcon without con to ret.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so, being relatively free of signature NPCs and metaplot events doesn't make the edition &quot;Continuity free&quot;. On the contrary it ret-cons or changes certain aspects of a game-line of which it is the continuation. I mean W20 and the Supplements aim to be the werewolf of the 2010s. How that will work out when White Wolf does a Werewolf 5th Edition we'll see.<br /> <br /> But in the meantime I feel that the W20 line doesn't do a good job to co-exist with the editions before and make people aware of changes and the reasons (in-setting and out of setting) that lead to these changes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=986932#post986932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get retconning to be annoying, and I agree with you on the stepping sideways issue (to a degree), but...<br /> [...]<br /> Yeah -- according to you. You've been banging the drum pretty hard that Kin can't do Rites for a long time, and anytime someone (like me, for instance) brings up evidence that seems to indicate that that's not <i>exactly</i> how it works, you ignore it and just keep insisting that you're right. Now the canon <i>specifically</i> states that it works more along the lines of &quot;yeah, but it's not a hard and fast rule and there are exceptions -- and here's a few of them...&quot;. Isn't it just <i>possible</i> that your interpretation wasn't entirely spot-on? Because this &quot;new&quot; take is how I've always read it from the very beginning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well &quot;While some Garou tribes allow Kinfolk to participate in or be present during the performance of rites, only Garou can successfully enact these ceremonies of the spirit.&quot;<br /> That's from PGtG page 127. I also remember a passage stating that Kinfolk can learn and teach rites and sometimes are chosen to protect knowledge, but I can't find it right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T14:35:39-07:00","id":989025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=988747#post988747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well &quot;While some Garou tribes allow Kinfolk to participate in or be present during the performance of rites, only Garou can successfully enact these ceremonies of the spirit.&quot;<br /> That's from PGtG page 127...</div> </div> </div> </div>Okaaaay... So... How <i>exactly</i> does that conflict with Morning Song? Like, all the other Rites need Garou participation to work (or are otherwise rituals that have no actual effect), and Morning Song is a Rite that specifically involves a Kin praising a spirit directly. If the spirit is pleased it <i>may</i> empower the Rite -- or not. Like, what's the issue?<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Garou are <i>not</i> enacting the Rite (as that quote states), as the culmination of the Rite involves the spiritual or magical effect. Yes, that's literally what that passage says, but when taken in the context of (pretty much) all other descriptions of how Rites work, that's not actually literally true. The <i>spirits</i> are the ones actually enacting (although I would use the phrase &quot;empowering) the Rite -- the Garou are simply performing it. What that passage really means is that only the Garou can perform a Rite and <i>expect</i> it to be empowered by the spirits. Kin cannot (as they are not party to The Great Spirit Pact).<br /> <br /> However, there's nothing that states (or even<i> implies</i>) that spirits <i>cannot</i> empower a Rite performed by Kin. There's plenty of passages that state that they generally <i>don't</i> -- but not &quot;can't&quot;. Moreover, the Rite of Sacred Rebirth (being a Rite performed by Kin, and having rather powerful spiritual effects) would imply that that's precisely how it works (since the Banes that generally empower<i> that </i>Rite, typically want to).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 10-17-2016, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T16:50:25-07:00","id":989615,"title":"","content":"Oh curious how difficult would it be for PC's to notice a FetchHawk, or parasitized kin Fetch?<br /> <br /> Also was thinking, what can a Silent Strider say, give a fianna or glasswalker Kinfolk in gratitude for board, as their not <i>obligated</i> to do so, strictly speaking.<br /> <br /> money, is possible, but seems rather boring, <br /> <br /> an IOU?<br /> <br /> any other ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 10-18-2016, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T08:10:29-07:00","id":989881,"title":"","content":"Yeah, we already had the discussion about the involvement of spirits in Rites. Point is that unless Numina were bought a Kin person is a human (or animal) with the sole exceptions that they are less affected by the Curse, not affected by Delirium and have a higher probability to bear shape shifter children. Now, the ability to enact rites comes in, that makes them even closer to sorcerers, without being sorcerers and father away from humans, despite the fact that they are supposed to be humans.<br /> <br /> I mean, what is the point of Rite write-ups if they don't have any effect. The whole affair on how spiritual, religious or magical kin people are or can be should have been handled very differently from write Rites for Kin.<br /> <br /> Same goes for Kin-variants of established gifts. It is just not something that was necessary, imo.<br /> I feel, it changes the dynamic from what it used to be way too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 10-19-2016, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T17:33:16-07:00","id":990707,"title":"","content":"I would actually say that Kinfolk are innately less human than sorcerers. They can have half-siblings that are animals for goodness sake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T07:31:05-07:00","id":990949,"title":"","content":"You don't actually need to be a kinfolk for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T17:20:32-07:00","id":991187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=986661#post986661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It was a hard rule, with an exception.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard rules, by definition, do not have an exception. If there's an exception, then it's NOT a hard rule. The fact that there is ANY exception at all simply proves that there are likely to be MORE exceptions. The Skindancer Rite is PROOF that Kin CAN perform some Rites successfully and have been able to do so since some time in Late 1st Edition/Early 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=986661#post986661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not to retcon, that there have been, all along, ways to do Rites, if garou are participation, or maybe even without - for normal kinfolk is a Retcon and I hate those.<br /> For me Retcons and Reboots destroyed Ultimate Marvel and the DC Universe - I hate it happening in Werewolf, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they didn't retcon. Unless you can point to a specific page number and reference in a specific book that says: &quot;Rites have never and will not work for kinfolk, ever&quot; or something VERY close in approximation, then your understanding of &quot;the truth&quot; of the setting was incorrect.<br /> <br /> This isn't unreasonable. It's something that White Wolf and Onyx Path BOTH have specifically done a lot of over the years. They suggest something isn't likely or possible in the FICTION of the characters' understanding of their own &quot;reality&quot;, but then prove that it very much is possible. They did it in Vampire with 14th and 15th Gen vampires and dhampyrs when they &quot;suggested&quot; that 13th Gen was the worst generation a vampire could be and that vamps couldn't have babies. They did this in Wraith and Mage and Vampire when they &quot;suggested&quot; that the Mnemosyne and the Ahl-i-Batin and the Cappadocians were all dead.<br /> <br /> This is just another case of them leaving themselves leeway in earlier publications that they then capitalized on in a fashion that actually makes the game more interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=989881#post989881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, what is the point of Rite write-ups if they don't have any effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh... I see. You don't like retcons that disagree with how you want things to be (based upon flawed reading/understanding) and ignore the retcons that do agree with you. Because when you say stuff like this, you're clearly ignoring a whole mess of rites that existed in 1st and 2nd ed that SPECIFICALLY &quot;don't have any effect.&quot; They're just something the Garou do. For example, a number of Seasonal Rites.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=986661#post986661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way the book handles Rites, and gitfts for that matter, is just kind of unsatifactory for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's cool. I mean, obviously, WW/OP isn't going to kick in your door and tell you that you're &quot;playing it wrong&quot; and take away your books if you choose to ignore this part of the game at your table.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't mean that your take on the Kinfolk ability to successfully perform Rites was EVER &quot;correct&quot; when dealing with the game-as-written. It just means that you don't like the official answer now that it's actually been revealed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12579-lordcrimson","name":"LordCrimson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T17:44:57-07:00","id":991193,"title":"","content":"Eh, I actually completely agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a>. Rites always have been just for Fera. Kinfolk have never been able to use them (they can go through the motions, but there isn't a roll since nothing supernatural can come of it) outside of the Rite of Sacred Rebirth, which specifically said it was an exception. The books made it pretty clear that only creatures part of The Pact (Fera) could enact Rites.<br /> Now people may or may not agree, but that doesn't mean (prior to this newest book) that you were correct. The previous books made this point fairly clearly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordCrimson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=991187#post991187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hard rules, by definition, do not have an exception. If there's an exception, then it's NOT a hard rule. The fact that there is ANY exception at all simply proves that there are likely to be MORE exceptions. The Skindancer Rite is PROOF that Kin CAN perform some Rites successfully and have been able to do so since some time in Late 1st Edition/Early 2nd Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Rite of Sacred Rebirth is proof that kinfolk can perform &quot;a&quot; Rite, not some. And it was made clear that this particular Rite was an exception.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordCrimson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=991187#post991187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But they didn't retcon. Unless you can point to a specific page number and reference in a specific book that says: &quot;Rites have never and will not work for kinfolk, ever&quot; or something VERY close in approximation, then your understanding of &quot;the truth&quot; of the setting was incorrect.</div> </div> </div> </div>And to quote heinrich (quoting the PGttG):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=988747#post988747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well &quot;While some Garou tribes allow Kinfolk to participate in or be present during the performance of rites, <u>only Garou can successfully enact these ceremonies of the spirit</u>.&quot;<br /> That's from PGtG page 127.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. That reads like exactly what you are looking for. I'm not sure how you can interpret that any other way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordCrimson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=991187#post991187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that doesn't mean that your take on the Kinfolk ability to successfully perform Rites was EVER &quot;correct&quot; when dealing with the game-as-written. It just means that you don't like the official answer now that it's actually been revealed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just another voice on the internet, but I do agree that his/her interpretation of it was the &quot;game-as-written&quot;. And now KABA has changed that. I don't mind so much, but it is a retcon imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T01:22:29-07:00","id":991305,"title":"","content":"Maybe they should have filed it under &quot;optional rules for giving kinfolk a bit more oomph if you want to play an all-kinfolk game or something.&quot; Forsaken did that with The Pack, which released recently enough that the Apocalypse guys probably didn't actually get the idea from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T07:47:28-07:00","id":991394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=991305#post991305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe they should have filed it under &quot;optional rules for giving kinfolk a bit more oomph if you want to play an all-kinfolk game or something.&quot; Forsaken did that with The Pack, which released recently enough that the Apocalypse guys probably didn't actually get the idea from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>This might be how I'm going to treat it anyways. There is little reason to have Kinfolk enacting Rites in a Werewolf game. In an all kinfolk game though, I can see it adding a lot more to the narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T13:50:38-07:00","id":991518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well &quot;While some Garou tribes allow Kinfolk to participate in or be present during the performance of rites, <u>only Garou can successfully enact these ceremonies of the spirit</u>.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=991193#post991193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Emphasis mine. That reads like exactly what you are looking for. I'm not sure how you can interpret that any other way.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYeah, only that passage is not actually literally true. The Garou <i>cannot</i> enact a rite. They can only perform it. Enacting it means empowering it, and <i>only</i> spirits can do that. For instance, there are certain places (for instance, Malfeas) where the spirits which are required to empower Rites are simply not present (nor<i> can </i>be), and Rites simply fail automatically -- in which case, Garou are most certainly <i>NOT</i> enacting the Rite. That passage was an inarticulate way of saying that only Garou (and other Fera) can perform a Rite and <i>expect</i> it to function (as per the Great Spirit Pact).<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat the Garou do with Rites and what Kinfolk do with Rites are fundamentally the same thing. The only difference is what the spirits do -- or what they're contractually obligated to do. And if spirits are generally disinclined to empower Rites performed by beings whom they are not obligated to do anything with, then yes, Rites <i>generally</i> do not work for those individuals. There is <i>nothing</i> anywhere that says that spirits <i>cannot</i> empower Rites performed by Kinfolk, however.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd if you think there is, then I would invite you to find me a passage anywhere that actually says that. (Not says &quot;don't&quot; -- says &quot;can't&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 10-22-2016, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T17:43:45-07:00","id":991622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=990949#post990949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't actually need to be a kinfolk for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do though. The children of Garou are either Garou or Kinfolk. In order to have cross-species siblings, you have to have a male Garou sire children on a female human and a female wolf (either mundane or Kinfolk).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T18:51:58-07:00","id":991650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=991622#post991622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do though. The children of Garou are either Garou or Kinfolk. In order to have cross-species siblings, you have to have a male Garou sire children on a female human and a female wolf (either mundane or Kinfolk).</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of Garou x non-kin, there's a possibility that the offspring won't be kin. Hence, Elfive's point stands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T19:12:29-07:00","id":991658,"title":"","content":"Really, is that a change from 20th edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T03:33:36-07:00","id":991795,"title":"","content":"Your totally human father shacks up with a female Lupus. Boom, your half brother's a dog. That's what I meant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T10:09:15-07:00","id":991888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=991795#post991795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your totally human father shacks up with a female Lupus. Boom, your half brother's a <b>dog</b>. That's what I meant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mistaking this case's hypothetical half brother for a dog outside of puppy-hood is liable to cost said case a hand and a lot of blood, at the very least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T12:26:11-07:00","id":992526,"title":"","content":"Ah, understood, I had not been thinking of the female Lupus angle. My, that would make for an interesting family reunion. Hm, do female Lupus have limited fertility like female wolves do (a week of estrus during the winter)? And is the pregnancy for a female Lupus equal in duration to that of a female wolf (two months)?<br /> <br /> It takes around three years for a wolf to reach adulthood, so I imagine that there would be some rather interesting social dynamics occurring within the household. The Lupus female would have to be with the wolf pup for around twelve hours a day during the first three months and, quite frankly, she would want to be with other wolves to allow for proper socialization. After the first three months, the wolf pup could be around humans and, because it would be Wolf Kinfolk, it would be more sapient than a normal wolf, allowing it to mimic domesticated behavior after its mother explained things to it. After age three, however, wild instincts would probably kick in and, while it would probably not be as dangerous as a normal wolf, it would probably be looking to joining with pack of wolves as soon as possible.<br /> <br /> Of course, if the pup ended up being a Garou, things could get very interesting. While the wolf pup would be less connected to its wild instincts because of its interaction with its human father, it would be quite familiar with human society and, to a certain extent, human technology. It might even consider its human father to be its true father, which would cause some weird social interactions, especially if the pup ended up being a female Garou. As far as I know, there is no particular incest taboo in Garou society that would prevent a lupine daughter from interbreeding with her human father (other than her lupine mother might kick her rear end).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T14:23:45-07:00","id":992569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=991193#post991193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I actually completely agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a>. Rites always have been just for Fera. Kinfolk have never been able to use them (they can go through the motions, but there isn't a roll since nothing supernatural can come of it) outside of the Rite of Sacred Rebirth, which specifically said it was an exception. The books made it pretty clear that only creatures part of The Pact (Fera) could enact Rites.<br /> Now people may or may not agree, but that doesn't mean (prior to this newest book) that you were correct. The previous books made this point fairly clearly.<br /> <br /> The Rite of Sacred Rebirth is proof that kinfolk can perform &quot;a&quot; Rite, not some. And it was made clear that this particular Rite was an exception.<br /> <br /> <br /> And to quote heinrich (quoting the PGttG):<br /> <br /> Emphasis mine. That reads like exactly what you are looking for. I'm not sure how you can interpret that any other way.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just another voice on the internet, but I do agree that his/her interpretation of it was the &quot;game-as-written&quot;. And now KABA has changed that. I don't mind so much, but it is a retcon imo.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yes, it WAS a retcon, it may have been for the best, as Id complained myself, rather loudly about how kinfolk are so weak next to ghouls or kinain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T08:44:28-07:00","id":992964,"title":"","content":"About &quot;the Rite&quot;. Well, it comes from &quot;the guy&quot;. First mentioned in Valkenbourg Foundation, it reads in the characters entry:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Thaumaturgy</b>: Samuel Haight knows several Thaumaturgic spells and rituals, most of which can be found in the Vampire: The Masquerade rulesbook. Movement of Mind 2, Lure of<br /> Flames 1, Weather Control 1. He also knows a rite: the Ritual of Sacred Rebirth. </div> </div> </div>Showing, that when first presented, the Rite, wasn't even a Rite, but a Blood Magic Ritual. In his 2nd edition appearance when the Skin Dancers were introduced in WoD:Outcasts, the write-up of the Ritual hadn't changed much. It wasn't until revised's PGttG that the Ritual was called a Rite and explicitly stated, that it could be used without knowledge in Thaumaturgy, although Rituals 5 and Rites 5 are mandatory for Skin Dancer characters.<br /> <br /> So, what White Wolf did in revised was to elaborate on Outcasts, by creating a foundation that allowed the skin dancers to exist, without the need for Vampire or Mage:Sorcerer revised as means to explain how this Ritual turned Rite would work, when all others didn't. And they did so by saying &quot;This Rite, just does just does work&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, I find of &quot;I want Skin Dancers in the Setting&quot; a fruitless example for an exemption of the &quot;Kinfolk can't enact Rites&quot; rule, for it wasn't intended to be that exception. The reason, that murderous practice is even a Rite is just so that authors could keep the Skin Dancers, without explaining to us who Haight was (for everyone hated him in revised era), without involving Sorcery, Vampire, Book of Mirrors infernalism rules or any other crossover mechanics that would make sense when it come to the unspeakable act to become a werewolf, but were all left out for sake of &quot;no crossover, please&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------<br /> <br /> I totally agree that Kin are weaker than ghouls. But I don't see the point. Kinfolk are also weaker than kinain or mages. Some kin can be sorcerers, but would one allow one sorcerer in an all-kin-chronicle? Psychics ?<br /> If one plays a Kin chronicle, the setting for that game was used to be that of the Unsung Heroes. People who are everyday Joes or Janes.<br /> There is, imo, no need for expanding gifts, reworking existing gifts into Kin-versions, not mentioning the original kin gifts, reprint the psi-stuff and Rites that do or do not bring magical effects.<br /> <br /> Sure, the book might have been shorter, but that wouldn't have bothered me. And I would have very much liked to see a statement: &quot;There are some Kinfolk, who learn magic or are born with psychic abilities. Those are rare amongst humans and only slightly more common amongst the Kenning Kin. <b>WoD20: Sorcerer and Psychics</b> will go into detail an provide unified mechanics for characters like this.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T11:36:12-07:00","id":993029,"title":"","content":"I think the Sorcerers and Psychics should be common among the Kinain and Kinfolk because they are already supernatural creatures. In addition, it would have been nice if they had made the Kinfolk more like the Kinain, giving them a bonus (beyond reproduction) from Pure Bred. Hm, I will go off and develop that right now...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T12:30:57-07:00","id":993040,"title":"","content":"Oh curious what kinds of things should get a &quot;Garou Favor&quot;<br /> <br /> just doing your duty wont do.<br /> <br /> Also that background doesnt seem good for a Kinfolk say whos kind enough to host a garou pack.<br /> <br /> even a relatively well behaved pack who trys to appreciate their host, probaly wont go out of their way for them<br /> <br /> but probaly will respond if theirs a break in... not sure what else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T20:08:17-07:00","id":993270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=992964#post992964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About &quot;the Rite&quot;. Well, it comes from &quot;the guy&quot;. First mentioned in Valkenbourg Foundation, it reads in the characters entry:<br /> <br /> Showing, that when first presented, the Rite, wasn't even a Rite, but a Blood Magic Ritual. In his 2nd edition appearance when the Skin Dancers were introduced in WoD:Outcasts, the write-up of the Ritual hadn't changed much. It wasn't until revised's PGttG that the Ritual was called a Rite and explicitly stated, that it could be used without knowledge in Thaumaturgy, although Rituals 5 and Rites 5 are mandatory for Skin Dancer characters.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's an outright ridiculous statement. You are purposefully misinterpreting an example from an adventure (not a RULE -- and from my reading of previous threads, you've used that argument yourself, so please stop using hypocritical arguments that you don't actually believe, see Jam Technology and Past Lives discussions). It was clearly not that they were saying it was Blood Magic; they were saying, for the sake of simplicity of gameplay and as a GM, that you can just use the rules from Vampire if you don't have the rules for Werewolf. Or Mage, for that matter.<br /> <br /> You're going out of your way to twist the actually written text to meet your own agenda. Which is fine for your own table (if you're GM anyway), but doesn't make it a fact.<br /> <br /> And while I disagree with Prince of Night on the retcon bit (again, see that whole portion of my post about vaguely-worded and/or in-character &quot;statements of fact&quot; in WoD products stemming from day 1 of V:tM 1st Edition), I definitely agree with him on the need to up-power Kin. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12579-lordcrimson","name":"LordCrimson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T20:32:10-07:00","id":993281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordCrimson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=993270#post993270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely agree with him on the need to up-power Kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am genuinely curious...why? I don't necessarily disagree, but I would like to hear why you think kinfolk need to be boosted in power?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T21:40:03-07:00","id":993309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordCrimson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=993270#post993270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an outright ridiculous statement. You are purposefully misinterpreting an example from an adventure (not a RULE -- and from my reading of previous threads, you've used that argument yourself, so please stop using hypocritical arguments that you don't actually believe, see Jam Technology and Past Lives discussions). It was clearly not that they were saying it was Blood Magic; they were saying, for the sake of simplicity of gameplay and as a GM, that you can just use the rules from Vampire if you don't have the rules for Werewolf. Or Mage, for that matter.<br /> <br /> You're going out of your way to twist the actually written text to meet your own agenda. Which is fine for your own table (if you're GM anyway), but doesn't make it a fact.<br /> <br /> And while I disagree with Prince of Night on the retcon bit (again, see that whole portion of my post about vaguely-worded and/or in-character &quot;statements of fact&quot; in WoD products stemming from day 1 of V:tM 1st Edition), I definitely agree with him on the need to up-power Kin.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have to agree with you on the having an agenda.<br /> <br /> CWOD have always tried converting powers in the game being played into something NPC Enemys can have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T23:16:14-07:00","id":993342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=993281#post993281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am genuinely curious...why? I don't necessarily disagree, but I would like to hear why you think kinfolk need to be boosted in power?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, two reasons, really.<br /> <br /> The first has already been mentioned by Prince of the Night: other than their immunity to the Delirium, Kin had no powers (Gifts were rare and Rites that could be relied upon were clearly not assumed to be standard); whereas ghouls, sorcerers, enchanted folk and all the other &quot;demi-mortal&quot; allies of each set of supernatural most assuredly do.<br /> <br /> But the other is purely within the limits of W:tA itself: the Kin have been portrayed as, literally, powerless in every way. Some people (for example: Heinrich) seem to think that the Kin should be slaves of the Garou that can be abused at will (regardless of how you want to spin the &quot;terminology the Garou use&quot;, it's still chattel slavery). It literally eliminates them as a plausible force that PCs should need to (at least occasionally) reckon with -- whether that be diplomatically or... er... martially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12579-lordcrimson","name":"LordCrimson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T01:55:28-07:00","id":993385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordCrimson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=993270#post993270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an outright ridiculous statement. You are purposefully misinterpreting an example from an adventure (not a RULE -- and from my reading of previous threads, you've used that argument yourself, so please stop using hypocritical arguments that you don't actually believe, see Jam Technology and Past Lives discussions). It was clearly not that they were saying it was Blood Magic; they were saying, for the sake of simplicity of gameplay and as a GM, that you can just use the rules from Vampire if you don't have the rules for Werewolf. Or Mage, for that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Rite/Ritual did originally appear in the NPC write-up of arguably the only person who knew the damn-thing back then. It wasn't fluff, it wasn't hear-say, it was the NPC write-up and it had rules it it, like some other NPC sections had two, if the NPC had unique abilities, like fetishes or rank 6 gifts.<br /> <br /> It wasn't that there was first the Rite and then the author of <i>Valkenburg</i> thought &quot;Well, let's make it easier and present it as Thauma, for simplicity.&quot; It was the other way round. There was this bad-ass guy, who was a ghoul and a sorcerer/Thauma-user in an era where mechanics were kind of fluid and he had a level 5 Ritual unique to him. It was later, that it appeared as a Rite, arguably for simplicities sake in Outcasts and PGttG. Should this transformation for simplicities sake open the door for all kind of Rites that Kinfolk can do? I think not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordCrimson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=993270#post993270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're going out of your way to twist the actually written text to meet your own agenda. Which is fine for your own table (if you're GM anyway), but doesn't make it a fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where?<br /> Before <i>Kinfolk - A Breed apart</i>, where did it say that Kinfolk could use Rites, other than this very specific Rite?<br /> There are mentions, that they can't, and as far as I recall even a statement that they can use garou rites as foci, if they have True Magick, but any effect will have to come from their spheres.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordCrimson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=993270#post993270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And while I disagree with Prince of Night on the retcon bit (again, see that whole portion of my post about vaguely-worded and/or in-character &quot;statements of fact&quot; in WoD products stemming from day 1 of V:tM 1st Edition), I definitely agree with him on the need to up-power Kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what purpose ?<br /> Does the WoD need more supernaturals ?<br /> Does it make Kin more attractive to play in a group with garou, where the Setting states that garou apart from some Glass Walker camp wouldn't let kin in on the fight for Gaia?<br /> Does it make Kin more attractive to play in an all-kin game when they have more access to super powers? Why not play Sorcerer or mage for such a game?<br /> Does it make Kin more worthy participants in a hypothetical pissing contests with ghouls and kinain or Strike Force 0 agents ?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the other is purely within the limits of W:tA itself: the Kin have been portrayed as, literally, powerless in every way. Some people (for example: Heinrich) seem to think that the Kin should be slaves of the Garou that can be abused at will (regardless of how you want to spin the &quot;terminology the Garou use&quot;, it's still chattel slavery). It literally eliminates them as a plausible force that PCs should need to (at least occasionally) reckon with -- whether that be diplomatically or... er... martially. </div> </div> </div>EXCUSE ME. Where did you get this impression?<br /> <br /> If you had read '<i>Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes</i>' or other Kinfolk descriptions, especially in revised, you would lie if you said kinfolk were described as powerless. Or slaves for that matter. Hell, a huge percentage of Kinfolk don't necessarily know or care about Garou and life normal lives completely slavery free, except for their need to pay taxes.<br /> And even the group that W20 know calls Kenning Kinfolk is by now means always dominated by the wishes of their garou brethren.<br /> <br /> And as far as powers go. Immunity to delirium and rare gifts aren't the only aspects of Kinfolk people.<br /> They are unaffected by the Curse and don't cause the Curse in humans or animals and can therefore attempt tasks Garou can't. Like interaction with human authorities, long term infiltration of organisations/enterprises suspected of wyrm collaboration.<br /> They also don't have usually duties that call them away for extended periods (umbral quests) or bad times (caern attack), allowing them to hold positions in the public eye, like public office.<br /> <br /> <br /> Kinfolk are normal people, and are supposed to be that way. Ghouls and Kinain and what not in the WoD, are not supposed to be normal and simply asking for them to be made equal just because they are supporting characters of the WoD major game lines is without merit. For Kinfolk characters serve their purpose in Werewolf by being normal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T02:02:46-07:00","id":993386,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12579-lordcrimson\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12579_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12579\" data-vbnamecard=\"12579\">LordCrimson</a><br /> And since you have been on the forum for just about a week, read through <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/115435-sept-positions\">Sept Positions</a> before making assumptions about how I think the role of Kinfolk within Garou society looks like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T06:47:43-07:00","id":993474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordCrimson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=993342#post993342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The first has already been mentioned by Prince of the Night: other than their immunity to the Delirium, Kin had no powers (Gifts were rare and Rites that could be relied upon were clearly not assumed to be standard); whereas ghouls, sorcerers, enchanted folk and all the other &quot;demi-mortal&quot; allies of each set of supernatural most assuredly do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally don't see the point in comparing them to other lines supporting characters. The Vampire/Ghoul power relationship should not be the Garou/Kinfolk relationship. Things don't have to be equal. If you wanted a game to compare it to, I would say the Hunter/Bystander dynamic comes closer, but in the end, the comparison is pointless. Those are different games. Different themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordCrimson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=993342#post993342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But the other is purely within the limits of W:tA itself: the Kin have been portrayed as, literally, powerless in every way. Some people (for example: Heinrich) seem to think that the Kin should be slaves of the Garou that can be abused at will (regardless of how you want to spin the &quot;terminology the Garou use&quot;, it's still chattel slavery). It literally eliminates them as a plausible force that PCs should need to (at least occasionally) reckon with -- whether that be diplomatically or... er... martially.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree that kinfolk are powerless and exist for the sole purpose of Garou to have sex with. I also disagree with the view that kinfolk are regularly abused. I suppose on that front, we see Kinfolk completely differently. From a ST point of view, Kinfolk help ground a game about cosmic evil destroying the universe in family. Kinfolk are your brothers, your parents, you aunts and uncles, nieces and nephews. From in game, some kinfolk are fully capable of taking care of themselves. But a great many of them need protection from enemies only the Garou can face.<br /> Having to head to work, I don;t have time atm for a longer explanation.<br /> In the end, I don't think having access to Rites does much to really boost their power level. It just changes background lord thematically. I'm not against it really. It doesn't make much of a difference overall. And if comparing games, having a couple of levels of Rites isn't going to do much to help a Kinfolk square off against a Ghoul or Sorcerer.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T14:01:05-07:00","id":993688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=993474#post993474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't agree that kinfolk are powerless and exist for the sole purpose of Garou to have sex with.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOnly that's exactly how they've always been written -- so much so that Kin who refuse to mate lose standing in that society. Now, &quot;sole purpose&quot;? No, as they are also to act as the Garou's agents in the human world... But that <i>still</i> remains their <i>secondary</i> role. And it also remains something that the Garou <i>expect</i> them to do without question -- and the Kin have little to no say in the matter.<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I also disagree with the view that kinfolk are regularly abused.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some Kin <i>are</i>. They're subjected to <i>regular</i> abuse by their Garou relations just as human abusers do. As such, the statement is accurate. Now, is the <i>average</i> Kin physically abused? Perhaps not. The issue is that they <i>can be</i>, and there is exactly zero recourse for them when they are -- in part because they are utterly powerless as written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T14:21:35-07:00","id":993700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=993688#post993688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bOnly that's exactly how they've always been written -- so much so that Kin who refuse to mate lose standing in that society. Now, &quot;sole purpose&quot;? No, as they are also to act as the Garou's agents in the human world... But that <i>still</i> remains their <i>secondary</i> role. And it also remains something that the Garou <i>expect</i> them to do without question -- and the Kin have little to no say in the matter.<br /> \u200b<br /> Some Kin <i>are</i>. They're subjected to <i>regular</i> abuse by their Garou relations just as human abusers do. As such, the statement is accurate. Now, is the <i>average</i> Kin physically abused? Perhaps not. The issue is that they <i>can be</i>, and there is exactly zero recourse for them when they are -- in part because they are utterly powerless as written.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In Kinfolk a breed apart we see &quot;Gaias Judges&quot; a secret society of kinfolk, who look like they could be cool protaganists or antaganists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T19:10:43-07:00","id":993834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=993688#post993688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bOnly that's exactly how they've always been written -- so much so that Kin who refuse to mate lose standing in that society. Now, &quot;sole purpose&quot;? No, as they are also to act as the Garou's agents in the human world... But that <i>still</i> remains their <i>secondary</i> role. And it also remains something that the Garou <i>expect</i> them to do without question -- and the Kin have little to no say in the matter.<br /> \u200b<br /> Some Kin <i>are</i>. They're subjected to <i>regular</i> abuse by their Garou relations just as human abusers do. As such, the statement is accurate. Now, is the <i>average</i> Kin physically abused? Perhaps not. The issue is that they <i>can be</i>, and there is exactly zero recourse for them when they are -- in part because they are utterly powerless as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>And as established a few times now, we obviously view Garou society fairly differently. The bulk of this isn't a worthwhile conversation for me to go through again. And I'm not of the opinion that abuse <i>never</i> occurs. That would be a silly stance to take. I just think that it happens a lot less often than you seem to.<br /> <br /> In any case, having access to a few Rites in no way alters the relationship between kin and Garou. It doesn't suddenly elevate them to a power level where (if this is they way you see their society to begin with) the dynamic really changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 10-26-2016, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T22:34:48-07:00","id":993899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=993834#post993834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And as established a few times now, we obviously view Garou society fairly differently. The bulk of this isn't a worthwhile conversation for me to go through again. And I'm not of the opinion that abuse <i>never</i> occurs. That would be a silly stance to take. I just think that it happens a lot less often than you seem to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Power imbalance =/= abuse. The potential is there, but it isn't necessary in a story. Garou are messy, complex monsters, but kin don't exist to be mere sex objects; that is a reductive and shallow read on the situation. Rather, kin exist to ground the Garou, to make them care and love humanity (I feel like I say this a lot, maybe I should put it in my signature).<br /> <br /> Only the fucked-up werewolves see their mates as sex toys and nothing more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 10-27-2016, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T04:54:50-07:00","id":993984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=993899#post993899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather, kin exist to ground the Garou, to make them care and love humanity (I feel like I say this a lot, maybe I should put it in my signature).</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you should. If there is another Kinfolk book some 10 years from now, maybe you make the chapter introduction quote.<br /> <br /> I agree with yours and idpersona's posts about the role kinfolk plays within the WtA Setting.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T05:02:35-07:00","id":993986,"title":"","content":"Kin also exists as curse free emissarys for the Garou who can hold Jobs, buy things etc with no one suspecting them of being anything but slightly eccentric.<br /> <br /> oh it s aid that a few kin still practice mortal religions.<br /> <br /> How many do you think would have a unitarian outlook?<br /> <br /> &quot;Enjoy practicing christmas, and are willing to go to church to meet people, but do not believe&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T05:27:18-07:00","id":993994,"title":"","content":"I think many Christian Kinfolk would follow Stewardship Ideology and would interpret Gaia as God. Since the principle message of Jesus was acceptance, love, and tolerance (similar to Buddhism and Taoism) Christianity is essentially a very flexible philosophical system (the rigidity comes in the form of denominational practices).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T06:09:05-07:00","id":994005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=993899#post993899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree. Power imbalance =/= abuse. The potential is there, but it isn't necessary in a story. Garou are messy, complex monsters, but kin don't exist to be mere sex objects; that is a reductive and shallow read on the situation. <u>Rather, kin exist to ground the Garou, to make them care and love humanity</u> (I feel like I say this a lot, maybe I should put it in my signature).<br /> <br /> Only the fucked-up werewolves see their mates as sex toys and nothing more.</div> </div> </div> </div>100% agreed. Especially the highlighted part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T00:58:36-07:00","id":994458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=993986#post993986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kin also exists as curse free ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they? Was that changed in W20? For I remember that they are <u>lesser affected by the Curse</u>, without any example or mechanics given.<br /> But this still means, that even kinfolk might tolerate a garou only for a short while. It's okay if daddy comes home and spends the weekend with the kinds, but he isn't moving in.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T02:47:42-07:00","id":994472,"title":"","content":"I think he means that the Kin can interact with humanity without having to worry about inflicting the Curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T02:55:58-07:00","id":994474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=993899#post993899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather, kin exist to ground the Garou, to make them care and love humanity...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">100% agreed. Especially the highlighted part.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b&quot;Care for and love humanity&quot;?! So the Impergium was, what? A great big, 3,000 year-long hug?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T04:00:32-07:00","id":994487,"title":"","content":"It's something that happened a long time ago that a lot of Garou regret.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T04:34:03-07:00","id":994493,"title":"","content":"&quot;to make them&quot; he said, meaning that Kinfolk only recently managed to do make the garou care and love for humanity.<br /> <br /> Who would have thought to blame the Kinfolk community for the garou shortcomings.<br /> <br /> But, there is a difference between the history of the setting, and the elements of the setting and the narrative reason these elements have to exist in the setting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T05:17:23-07:00","id":994505,"title":"","content":"id prefer to think that kinfolk exist as a bridge between the garou and humanity, not to MAKE the garou do anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T06:54:13-07:00","id":994540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=994505#post994505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">id prefer to think that kinfolk exist as a bridge between the garou and humanity, not to MAKE the garou do anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the same effect. In game, Kinfolk aren't <i>making</i> the Garou care about humanity. Narratively though, that is the role they play.<br /> <br /> Family doesn't <i>make</i> you care about them. But having family invests/grounds you in their wellbeing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T07:33:40-07:00","id":994564,"title":"","content":"ok specifically Im thinking they hold jobs, go to school do other &quot;Normal Stuff&quot;<br /> <br /> oh it mentions thin in book of the city<br /> <br /> how hard would it be for a homid to finish high school? &quot;Think buffy the wyrmslayer and your on the right track&quot; it said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T07:44:58-07:00","id":994572,"title":"","content":"Well, a very low Rage (Rage 1-2) Homid Garou could potentially have sufficient self-control to finish high school without killing anyone (they would also find themselves as the caretaker of the local Human Kinfolk because they would be really hard to drive into a frenzy). A very low Homid Garou that maintained such a low Rage would probably find themselves relegated to Human Kinfolk management for a large geographical region (and a very low Rage male Homid Garou would find himself having a lot of opportunities to engage in sex with a lot of female Human Kinfolk because he would be warm and cuddly in comparison to other male Garou). Strangely enough, they would have a reproductive advantage over higher Rage Homid Garou because they would just be approachable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 10-28-2016, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T08:39:50-07:00","id":994611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=994474#post994474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b&quot;Care for and love humanity&quot;?! So the Impergium was, what? A great big, 3,000 year-long hug?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is like arguing that a Mongolian guy shouldn't marry a Polish woman because of the Hun invasion.<br /> <br /> Circumstances change, and we are not our ancestors. The same is true of the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 10-28-2016, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T08:52:27-07:00","id":994618,"title":"","content":"Reasonable.<br /> <br /> as to Those with Moderately low Rage 3-5? <br /> <br /> probaly unlikely I know<br /> <br /> Oh how do Social attributes and the Curse even out? <br /> <br /> someone with Charisma 4 Appearance 5 Man 3, Rage 8, whats it like when you can see that their beautiful and charismatic but can FEEL danger radiating from them..<br /> <br /> My attidue is the results of the roll will likely stand but you'll have to make a LOT of rolls you can probaly convince someone to do you favors or to trust you, but they wont approach you of their own initiative, likely not even if they've come to think of you as a friend, they might acceept your presence and enjoy your conversation.<br /> <br /> Incidently I was a bit of an outcast in highschool, and junior high and gradeschool, I still survied to get my diploma.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Another thing I just noticed is the Intuition Talent in its &quot;Possesed by&quot; It says Kinfolk, counselors, mothers, trending experts, teachers, intuitive diagnosticians, private detectives.<br /> <br /> sounds like its available to nonkinfolk.<br /> <br /> had alwaysd thought that it represented a vestigial bestial aspect of a Kinfolk","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:28:42-07:00","id":994658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=994572#post994572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, a very low Rage (Rage 1-2) Homid Garou could potentially have sufficient self-control to finish high school without killing anyone</div> </div> </div> </div>Rage rating alone does not determine self control. A Garou could have 8 Rage and as long as long as they have a higher Willpower, they could be unlikely to Frenzy. Obviously though, the lower the Rage and higher the Willpower, the less chance they will have. But basin the assumption purely on Rage is misleading.<br /> The Curse is a bigger impediment than the risk of Frenzy when talking about finishing high school, or engaging in any other &quot;normal&quot; social situation/activity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=994572#post994572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (they would also find themselves as the caretaker of the local Human Kinfolk because they would be really hard to drive into a frenzy). A very low Homid Garou that maintained such a low Rage would probably find themselves relegated to Human Kinfolk management for a large geographical region</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are there Garou monitors for kinfolk? That isn't a role someone gets assigned to. Kinfolk are perfectly capable (and should be expected to) &quot;manage&quot; themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=994572#post994572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(and a very low Rage male Homid Garou would find himself having a lot of opportunities to engage in sex with a lot of female Human Kinfolk because he would be warm and cuddly in comparison to other male Garou). Strangely enough, they would have a reproductive advantage over higher Rage Homid Garou because they would just be approachable.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is so much wrong with this line of thought, I'm not sure where to start. This is a creepy and flawed outlook in general (imo) and it makes assumptions on what people look for in a mate that I don't think actually pan out. Either way though, it isn't really a point worth debating I don't think.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=994618#post994618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh how do Social attributes and the Curse even out?<br /> <br /> someone with Charisma 4 Appearance 5 Man 3, Rage 8, whats it like when you can see that their beautiful and charismatic but can FEEL danger radiating from them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rage 8 means that 93% of the population is going to assume you are dangerous just by looking at you. Sure, you can try and overcome that through social interaction, but at first glace, most people will assume the worst, and generally avoid you. And that effect will always be there. The Curse doesn't go away with time either. Even when you've earned someone's trust, they will always know/suspect that you might snap and hurt them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=994618#post994618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Another thing I just noticed is the Intuition Talent in its &quot;Possesed by&quot; It says Kinfolk, counselors, mothers, trending experts, teachers, intuitive diagnosticians, private detectives.<br /> <br /> sounds like its available to nonkinfolk.<br /> <br /> had alwaysd thought that it represented a vestigial bestial aspect of a Kinfolk</div> </div> </div> </div>Intuition has always been available to Mortals as far as I can remember. It isn't so much a &quot;bestial aspect&quot;, as normal human instincts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 10-28-2016, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:02:38-07:00","id":994813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=994611#post994611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is like arguing that a Mongolian guy shouldn't marry a Polish woman because of the Hun invasion.<br /> <br /> Circumstances change, and we are not our ancestors. The same is true of the Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, yeah... because the Garou have <i>totally</i> changed. The last time they pulled that kind of garbage was the War of Tears and that was waaaaaaay back -- in the 1930s. Y'know, within living memory.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's something that happened a long time ago that a lot of Garou regret.</div> </div> </div> </div> And that a lot of Garou <i>don't</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:06:38-07:00","id":994818,"title":"","content":"The impergium was closer to a flogging, then a hug to be honest, was about to saay spanking, but felt that would trivialize it.<br /> <br /> It was a way of communicating &quot;Dont do that!!!&quot; but it obviously backfired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:39:53-07:00","id":994851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=994813#post994813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh, yeah... because the Garou have <i>totally</i> changed. The last time they pulled that kind of garbage was the War of Tears and that was waaaaaaay back -- in the 1930s. Y'know, within living memory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Current events could easily have caused an unprecedented direction of moving toward change, what with the scale of conflicts, technology involved, threat of nuclear annihilation, etc. The key to surviving is for Garou who are convinced of the need for a new game plan to convince others that it isn't against their nature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200b And that a lot of Garou <i>don't</i>. </div> </div> </div>They're the smallest tribe, and a minority of loose associates in a few others. The party line is that it was a mistake, or else it would have been made part of their normal policy when the Litany was handed down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T20:53:47-07:00","id":995051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=994851#post994851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Current events could easily have caused an unprecedented direction of moving toward change...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! <i>Unprecedented</i>. That's sort of <i>exactly</i> my point.<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...what with the scale of conflicts, technology involved, threat of nuclear annihilation, etc. The key to surviving is for Garou who are convinced of the need for a new game plan to convince others that it isn't against their nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAnd...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're the smallest tribe, and a minority of loose associates in a few others. The party line is that it was a mistake, or else it would have been made part of their normal policy when the Litany was handed down.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe Get, the Shadow Lords, the Wendigo, the Uktena, and the Black Furies are hardly <i>small</i> tribes. Moreover, the Garou in those tribes, plus the Silver Fangs, and Fianna who <i>do</i> &quot;regret&quot; the Impergium, do so <i>not</i> because they feel it was in any way immoral or wrong, but rather because (as you just mentioned yourself) it's becoming painfully obvious in the span of the last century to all but the densest Garou that it simply didn't turn out the way the Garou Nation wanted.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe &quot;party line&quot; as you say, is that the Impergium was &quot;wrong&quot; only because it made the situation worse, and that if instead it had left humanity properly cowed and &quot;in their place&quot; (presumably huddling in caves and only venturing out to gather nuts, berries, roots, and grubs when starvation motivated them to risk the horrible wolf-monsters outside), that would have been perfectly acceptable. (Save for the Children and the Glass Walkers and a few others).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 10-28-2016, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T22:48:50-07:00","id":995087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=995051#post995051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes! <i>Unprecedented</i>. That's sort of <i>exactly</i> my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the context of past events. Now, it is precedented.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bAnd...<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Get, the Shadow Lords, the Wendigo, the Uktena, and the Black Furies are hardly <i>small</i> tribes. </div> </div> </div>The Pure Tribes never participated in the Impergium, and wouldn't advocate a return to it. The Black Furies tend to stand against it, too. This leaves you with a moderately-sized tribe obsessed with hierarchy and naysaying the Fangs' dictates, and the fringe extremist groups of the Get and Fianna.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Moreover, the Garou in those tribes, plus the Silver Fangs, and Fianna who <i>do</i> &quot;regret&quot; the Impergium, do so <i>not</i> because they feel it was in any way immoral or wrong, but rather because (as you just mentioned yourself) it's becoming painfully obvious in the span of the last century to all but the densest Garou that it simply didn't turn out the way the Garou Nation wanted. </div> </div> </div>The Fianna are as stuck to their human kin as one can possibly be, on a level that only the Hakken can surpass. Only the Eire/Gaia's Fundamentalists actually view the Impergium in rose-colored glasses. The original reason, incidentally, that it ended, is because the Garou had a big debate before human civilization started and decided to stop systematically terrorizing and killing humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bThe &quot;party line&quot; as you say, is that the Impergium was &quot;wrong&quot; only because it made the situation worse, and that if instead it had left humanity properly cowed and &quot;in their place&quot; (presumably huddling in caves and only venturing out to gather nuts, berries, roots, and grubs when starvation motivated them to risk the horrible wolf-monsters outside), that would have been perfectly acceptable. (Save for the Children and the Glass Walkers and a few others). </div> </div> </div>No, again, debate, the pro-Impergium side lost, and everyone has been told this for millennia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T03:11:21-07:00","id":995135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=995087#post995087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Pure Tribes never participated in the Impergium, and wouldn't advocate a return to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b&quot;...They planted the lust for these things into the waischu, who then broke all their promises and stole more land so they could rape the earth for these treasures. And still they do these things. When will they stop? Only when we kill them all. Only after every one of them is dead will the earth again be safe. They must die for what they have done!&quot; Da-jo-ji (the West Wind) describes his solution to white people. Wendigo page 28.<br /> <br /> Uh-huh. Oh, and just for the record, that isn't some Ahroun cliath either. That's one of the top four totems of the tribe.<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Black Furies tend to stand against it, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThere is no tribe closer to the Red Talons than the Furies, and ever since &quot;The Burning Times&quot;, and the rise of The Patriarch, their views of modern human society has hardened significantly. Their views tend to not go so far as outright extermination of the human race, but they do advocate taking modern technological society down a few notches.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This leaves you with a moderately-sized tribe obsessed with hierarchy and naysaying the Fangs' dictates, and the fringe extremist groups of the Get and Fianna..</div> </div> </div> </div> The pro-killing-people segment of the Get of Fenris is a &quot;fringe group&quot;?<br /> <br /> \u200bUh-huh.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T07:35:35-07:00","id":995189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=995135#post995135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b&quot;...They planted the lust for these things into the waischu, who then broke all their promises and stole more land so they could rape the earth for these treasures. And still they do these things. When will they stop? Only when we kill them all. Only after every one of them is dead will the earth again be safe. They must die for what they have done!&quot; Da-jo-ji (the West Wind) describes his solution to white people. Wendigo page 28.<br /> <br /> Uh-huh. Oh, and just for the record, that isn't some Ahroun cliath either. That's one of the top four totems of the tribe.<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200bThere is no tribe closer to the Red Talons than the Furies, and ever since &quot;The Burning Times&quot;, and the rise of The Patriarch, their views of modern human society has hardened significantly. Their views tend to not go so far as outright extermination of the human race, but they do advocate taking modern technological society down a few notches.<br /> The pro-killing-people segment of the Get of Fenris is a &quot;fringe group&quot;?<br /> <br /> \u200bUh-huh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could someone explain to me how I Break up a post into replying to one thing at a time?<br /> <br /> I'd agree the Get of fenris willing to kill people are NOT a fringe group.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T07:59:06-07:00","id":995195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=995135#post995135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b&quot;...They planted the lust for these things into the waischu, who then broke all their promises and stole more land so they could rape the earth for these treasures. And still they do these things. When will they stop? Only when we kill them all. Only after every one of them is dead will the earth again be safe. They must die for what they have done!&quot; Da-jo-ji (the West Wind) describes his solution to white people. Wendigo page 28.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wendigo have traditionally hated the &quot;White Man&quot;/Wyrmcomers. That doesn't mean they want to cull all of humanity again (bringing back the Impergium). Sorry, but to me, that example fails to support your claim.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=995135#post995135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200bThere is no tribe closer to the Red Talons than the Furies, and ever since &quot;The Burning Times&quot;, and the rise of The Patriarch, their views of modern human society has hardened significantly. Their views tend to not go so far as outright extermination of the human race, but they do advocate taking modern technological society down a few notches.</div> </div> </div> </div> Most of the Fury tribal goals are seating firming in the idea of uplifting (sections of) Humanity. You aren't going to get any but the possibly most extreme/unhinged of them to sign up for genocide. And taking the Weaver down a few notches in no way equates to bringing back the Impergium. Again, to me, this fails to support your claim.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=995189#post995189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could someone explain to me how I Break up a post into replying to one thing at a time?</div> </div> </div> </div>I copy/paste the beginning and end quote brackets around whichever part I'm replying to.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=995189#post995189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd agree the Get of fenris willing to kill people are NOT a fringe group.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't a matter of Get being willing to kill. The Get in general do not advocate genocide of the human race (which is what talk of bringing back the Impergium amounts to). That is something completely different. The only Tribe that generally view this prospect as a good thing is the Talons. And even they have a camp that is firmly against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T08:17:03-07:00","id":995206,"title":"","content":"The Impergium was a bad idea. Ending it may have made things even worse, but trying to start it again <i>now</i> will almost certainly make things <i>even worse. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T08:19:24-07:00","id":995208,"title":"","content":"The question is not whether the Garou want to return to the Imperium its whether they can return to the Imperium. The Garou are outnumbered 1:500,000 and, while they are really good at killing people, they would be killed off long before they could kill off 1% of humanity. The only sure way to kill off the majority of humans would be a nuclear holocaust, which would cause the Wyrm to dance with glee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T08:19:47-07:00","id":995209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=995195#post995195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This isn't a matter of Get being willing to kill. The Get in general do not advocate genocide of the human race (which is what talk of bringing back the Impergium amounts to). That is something completely different. The only Tribe that generally view this prospect as a good thing is the Talons. And even they have a camp that is firmly against it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Even many of whelps compromise might welcome a new impergium just dont think it needs to be as complete as the predator kings or dieing cubs think it does.<br /> <br /> They may stalk try to &quot;Educate&quot; a human but remove him, so he doesnt teach other humans bad habits if it seems to be in vain.<br /> <br /> many of the Warders of the Land are also firmly against a new impergium... though many just dont think they have the means to do so.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T15:08:49-07:00","id":995372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=995195#post995195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wendigo have traditionally hated the &quot;White Man&quot;/Wyrmcomers. That doesn't mean they want to cull all of humanity again (bringing back the Impergium). Sorry, but to me, that example fails to support your claim.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOkay, so let's say that Native Americans are (pulling a number out of thin air) say, 5% of the population of North America. So the Wendigo are willing to brutally murder the other 95% and burn their cities to the ground, but leave Europe and the rest of the world alone (since that's not their traditional stomping ground) -- then that's fundamentally different from &quot;the Impergium&quot; somehow?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the Fury tribal goals are seating firming in the idea of uplifting (sections of) Humanity. You aren't going to get any but the possibly most extreme/unhinged of them to sign up for genocide. And taking the Weaver down a few notches in no way equates to bringing back the Impergium. Again, to me, this fails to support your claim.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI didn't say &quot;the Weaver&quot;, I said &quot;modern technological society&quot;. Now, while the Furies might see the two as one and the same, there's a critical distinction in there. Forcibly reducing the levels of technology in human society to what it was before the Industrial Revolution and forcibly reorganizing that society so that the traditional male dominance (which is slowly being eroded on its own, by the way) is destroyed, implicitly involves a level of bloodshed that hasn't been seen since the Second World War.<br /> <br /> \u200bJust because they aren't going to call it &quot;the Impergium&quot; doesn't somehow make it any different in reality.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't a matter of Get being willing to kill. The Get in general do not advocate genocide of the human race (which is what talk of bringing back the Impergium amounts to).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b&quot;From him... &quot;(Great Fenris)&quot; ...we learned how best to cull the flocks of humans. Humans fell before us, victims of the Impergium...&quot; &quot;...We have tolerated the dilution of the truth among the humans for the sake of the Concord. I can see it in your eyes... you feel that the Concord was a mistake. Many agree with you, but the decision was made before our time of power.&quot; Get of Fenris, pages 15-16.<br /> \u200b&quot;Ragnarok is upon us, and the time for friendship is past. Those who would flee from us must be destroyed, for surely they would fall to Jormangundr's wiles. Those that would fight us must be taught the error of their ways, and those who would ignore us must be made to remember that we are here, no matter the cost.&quot; &quot;Ragnarok is when Great Fenris will finally be freed from the chains that hold him back, where the Wolf will again know the taste of raw meat and the feel of bones shattering beneath his awesome fangs. We are the Get of Fenris, the children of the Dire Wolf. Fenris will be released, and as our own sayings tell, he will call forth the Fenris Winter, called the Fimbul Winter by the humans, and he will slay Wotan, the greatest of the Viking gods. But let us not forget that the Vikings, despite their many admirable qualities, were only human. Because they did not understand the meaning of Wotan, they could not understand the necessity for his destruction. He was the greatest of their gods, but he is also a bringer of death. Wotan is another name for Man. He is a god of the humans. The prophecies say simply that Fenris will destroy the humans. The most likely means for this destruction is, of course, the Get of Fenris. In the last few decades, almost all signs from the Rite of Three Wells have revealed the same image again and again...&quot; &quot;... The image shows Fenris consuming Wotan. Both comprise countless thousands of beings: Fenris is an amalgamation of our tribe, and Wotan contains the sum of humanity...&quot; Get of Fenris, page 22.<br /> \u200bAnd before you start going off about &quot;fringe elements&quot;, this guy is Mjolnir's Thunder, not Glorious Fist of Wotan. This is the friggin' tribe.<br /> <br /> \u200bHe also goes on to say that while this might be symbolic only, and may only mean that the Get will be the cause of the end of human domination of the planet -- that's not terribly clear; the relish with which it's rattled off indicates otherwise, and it also glosses over if it's only meant to be symbolic, exactly how taking down human society without countless deaths is going to happen. (The demise of modern agriculture would, in itself, incur a death toll in the millions).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 11-02-2016, 04:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T15:59:03-07:00","id":995400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=995372#post995372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Snip...</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a post written out with responses to each section of this but it got eaten by the internet and I don't feel like re-typing it. You seem fairly cemented in your views and I disagree with them. Garou are prone to vendettas and hatreds (as warrior cultures are) and that is fine. In setting, inarguably, Humanity is the cause of a lot of the world's (and thus Gaia's) suffering and they could use having a drastic population reduction. Even with that said, I disagree with your assessment that most Garou support bringing back the Impergium. You also seem to equate any population reduction spouted by any Elder of any tribe as the Tribe supporting the Impergium. I disagree with that as well.<br /> <br /> The only tribe that has regularly touted the idea of bringing the Impergium back is the Talons. And they are a tiny (probably the smallest, equal with the Stargazers) Tribe who don't actually get a real say in the overall Garou Nation. So the Impergium isn't going to be brought back, at all.<br /> <br /> Come the Apocalypse, Humanity is going to suffer innumerable casualties. That is the nature of a world ending event. It does not mean Garou have brought back the Impergium. Even if the Get, <i>during the end of the world</i>, kill all humans, that still wouldn't be them bringing back the Impergium. That would be the world ending. That's all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 10-29-2016, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T16:22:36-07:00","id":995416,"title":"","content":"Native Americans are around 1% of the population of the USA (with another 1% having enough Native American blood to be considered 'mixed'). While the majority of the Hispanic population possesses Indigenous Mexican blood, they are not considered to be part of the Native American people of the USA. Likewise, the majority of African Americans and European Americans have some Native American blood, the vast majority cannot claim more than 1/64.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T20:12:40-07:00","id":995932,"title":"","content":"oh on kinfolk in general Ideas on how they could use Supernatural 