geshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 11-01-2016, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T16:23:09-07:00","id":996872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=995400#post995400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a post written out with responses to each section of this but it got eaten by the internet and I don't feel like re-typing it. You seem fairly cemented in your views and I disagree with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fine that you disagree, but your &quot;argument&quot; as to why others are &quot;wrong&quot; amounts to you saying &quot;nuh-uh&quot; over and over again rather than actually presenting any actual evidence from the text to support your opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=995400#post995400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Even with that said, I disagree with your assessment that most Garou support bringing back the Impergium. You also seem to equate any population reduction spouted by any Elder of any tribe as the Tribe supporting the Impergium. I disagree with that as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that his quotes are coming directly from the tribebooks which exist to portray what the &quot;average&quot; tribe member is like. You're claiming that the books that exist SOLELY to portray the definitive archetypes of what those tribes believe aren't accurate portrayals. So what resources/references are you appealing to in order to back that claim?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=995400#post995400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only tribe that has regularly touted the idea of bringing the Impergium back is the Talons. And they are a tiny (probably the smallest, equal with the Stargazers) Tribe who don't actually get a real say in the overall Garou Nation. So the Impergium isn't going to be brought back, at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're the only tribe that is regularly touted because their the only tribe where the VAST MAJORITY of the tribe believe it. For all the other tribes, they only need 49.9% for their members to be pro-Impergium for it to still be a minority... but even if it's &quot;only&quot; 25% that's STILL a SIZABLE minority. Especially when one whole tribe (Talons) pretty much buys into it whole-hog.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=995400#post995400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Come the Apocalypse, Humanity is going to suffer innumerable casualties. That is the nature of a world ending event. It does not mean Garou have brought back the Impergium. Even if the Get, <i>during the end of the world</i>, kill all humans, that still wouldn't be them bringing back the Impergium. That would be the world ending. That's all.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's not what this representative &quot;fairly moderate camp&quot; member is saying. He's not claiming that &quot;when our foe rises, a bunch of people will get killed.&quot; He's saying &quot;WE (as the body and hand of Fenris) will exterminate humankind.&quot;<br /> <br /> You can split hairs all you want, but just because they're calling that the Apocalypse doesn't change the fact that it's just the Impergium under another name and religious justification.<br /> <br /> The Garou are MONSTERS who are dissociated from Humanity. To try to pretend that they're somehow exempt from the rest of the WoD's pessimistic worldview of corrupted power, corrupted faith, and the exploitation of the weak is willfully ignoring several of the primary themes of the ENTIRE game line simply because it paints your favorite splat in a negative light that makes you uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> So while that is fine at your own table, it still contradicts with how the Garou are being ACTIVELY and CONSISTENTLY represented by the writers of the game line as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12579-lordcrimson","name":"LordCrimson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T16:56:20-07:00","id":996886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordCrimson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=996872#post996872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's fine that you disagree, but your &quot;argument&quot; as to why others are &quot;wrong&quot; amounts to you saying &quot;nuh-uh&quot; over and over again rather than actually presenting any actual evidence from the text to support your opinion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Except that his quotes are coming directly from the tribebooks which exist to portray what the &quot;average&quot; tribe member is like. You're claiming that the books that exist SOLELY to portray the definitive archetypes of what those tribes believe aren't accurate portrayals. So what resources/references are you appealing to in order to back that claim?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They're the only tribe that is regularly touted because their the only tribe where the VAST MAJORITY of the tribe believe it. For all the other tribes, they only need 49.9% for their members to be pro-Impergium for it to still be a minority... but even if it's &quot;only&quot; 25% that's STILL a SIZABLE minority. Especially when one whole tribe (Talons) pretty much buys into it whole-hog.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But that's not what this representative &quot;fairly moderate camp&quot; member is saying. He's not claiming that &quot;when our foe rises, a bunch of people will get killed.&quot; He's saying &quot;WE (as the body and hand of Fenris) will exterminate humankind.&quot;<br /> <br /> You can split hairs all you want, but just because they're calling that the Apocalypse doesn't change the fact that it's just the Impergium under another name and religious justification.<br /> <br /> The Garou are MONSTERS who are dissociated from Humanity. To try to pretend that they're somehow exempt from the rest of the WoD's pessimistic worldview of corrupted power, corrupted faith, and the exploitation of the weak is willfully ignoring several of the primary themes of the ENTIRE game line simply because it paints your favorite splat in a negative light that makes you uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> So while that is fine at your own table, it still contradicts with how the Garou are being ACTIVELY and CONSISTENTLY represented by the writers of the game line as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll only say it once.<br /> <br /> Nuh-uh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T17:03:14-07:00","id":996890,"title":"","content":"In all seriousness, most modern Garou are homid; the vast majority of most tribes have dwindling numbers of lupus. Which means that by extension, most werewolves have human mothers or fathers, and human siblings. They will very likely have human children. And now I am supposed to believe that most of them would want to impose a neo-Impergium? Yeah right. The Talons are viewed as marginalized extremists for a reason- because their utopia excludes the families of the other Garou.<br /> <br /> A few cherry-picked quotes from some tribebooks isn't enough to support otherwise.<br /> <br /> The Garou, like it or not, have changed since prehistory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 11-01-2016, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T17:38:14-07:00","id":996903,"title":"","content":"true to a degree but the shadow lord who spoke in the red talon tribe book<br /> &quot;Malcom the liar&quot; I dont think he was lieing when he said the talons were right about the impergium ending it was a mistake.<br /> <br /> I think that if the garou win the apocalypse MANY including some homids, might demand a new impergium.<br /> <br /> Hmmmn any ideas again how Kin with resources would pay tribute to the sept?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 11-01-2016, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T18:03:15-07:00","id":996911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=996903#post996903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">true to a degree but the shadow lord who spoke in the red talon tribe book<br /> &quot;Malcom the liar&quot; I dont think he was lieing when he said the talons were right about the impergium ending it was a mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the Shadow Lords' thing. But they're also political, so they could just as easily be against the Impergium, depending on the circumstances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that if the garou win the apocalypse MANY including some homids, might demand a new impergium.<br /> <br /> Hmmmn any ideas again how Kin with resources would pay tribute to the sept? </div> </div> </div>Garou victory would significantly alter what the world looks like, to the point where all previous plans would have to be redrawn extensively. And given the tales of the ending of the Impergium, it's not likely to restart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T18:36:05-07:00","id":996921,"title":"","content":"I think we've accomplished all were going to debating the impergium? Thoughts on how many kinfolk will live in the wilderness or as the garous eyes and ears in the city","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 11-01-2016, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T21:33:43-07:00","id":996998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordCrimson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=996872#post996872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's fine that you disagree, but your &quot;argument&quot; as to why others are &quot;wrong&quot; amounts to you saying &quot;nuh-uh&quot; over and over again rather than actually presenting any actual evidence from the text to support your opinion.<br /> <br /> Except that his quotes are coming directly from the tribebooks which exist to portray what the &quot;average&quot; tribe member is like. You're claiming that the books that exist SOLELY to portray the definitive archetypes of what those tribes believe aren't accurate portrayals. So what resources/references are you appealing to in order to back that claim?</div> </div> </div> </div>To back my claims, I generally draw from 2 decades of playing the games (mainly Werewolf and Vampire). I do not feel the need to go back through a few dozen books to cite page numbers generally. Discussion on the forums (for me) and for fun and mutual interest. This isn't a thesis paper. Apologies if that isn't enough, feel free to ignore my posts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordCrimson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=996872#post996872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They're the only tribe that is regularly touted because their the only tribe where the VAST MAJORITY of the tribe believe it. For all the other tribes, they only need 49.9% for their members to be pro-Impergium for it to still be a minority... but even if it's &quot;only&quot; 25% that's STILL a SIZABLE minority. Especially when one whole tribe (Talons) pretty much buys into it whole-hog.</div> </div> </div> </div>Homids make up 75-85% of the Garou population in the modern era, depending on the book you go by. I cannot see Homids supporting bringing back the Impergium. It doesn't make any sense. Talons can support the idea, because it doesn't affect their families at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordCrimson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=996872#post996872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But that's not what this representative &quot;fairly moderate camp&quot; member is saying. He's not claiming that &quot;when our foe rises, a bunch of people will get killed.&quot; He's saying &quot;WE (as the body and hand of Fenris) will exterminate humankind.&quot;<br /> <br /> You can split hairs all you want, but just because they're calling that the Apocalypse doesn't change the fact that it's just the Impergium under another name and religious justification.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what do you think the Impergium is? It isn't wholesale slaughter. It is/was systematic and prolonged culling/terrorizing of humankind to keep their numbers down. If a group of Garou manage to kill 90% of humanity, that still wouldn't be &quot;an&quot; Impergium. At this point, I feel like the term Impergium is being used by some to just mean a war/slaughter of Humanity, when it is so much more complicated than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordCrimson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=996872#post996872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Garou are MONSTERS who are dissociated from Humanity. To try to pretend that they're somehow exempt from the rest of the WoD's pessimistic worldview of corrupted power, corrupted faith, and the exploitation of the weak is willfully ignoring several of the primary themes of the ENTIRE game line simply because it paints your favorite splat in a negative light that makes you uncomfortable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am fine with Garou having negative aspects to them. I know that they're monsters. But what you just said goes against <i>some</i> of the themes of the game. Werewolf, to me, is about tragic heroes. The game is at least somewhat about hope. About fighting against all odds to save a world that arguably doesn't want to be saved. It shouldn't be overly pessimistic. That misses the point. As for the corruption angle, I can certainly agree that some Garou end up corrupted. Assuming all power and faith corrupts though, completely misses the point of the game imo. Because they understand that they are fighting corruption incarnate (the Wyrm), the Garou can and do take steps to make themselves somewhat less prone to said corruption.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordCrimson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=996872#post996872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So while that is fine at your own table, it still contradicts with how the Garou are being ACTIVELY and CONSISTENTLY represented by the writers of the game line as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot accept that argument, as you failed to cite a book and page reference.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In the end, I am fine disagreeing on the details of the game. It makes zero difference. There is no such need on my end to convince you that I'm right. Enjoy the game as you see fit.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T21:42:28-07:00","id":997002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=996921#post996921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we've accomplished all were going to debating the impergium? Thoughts on how many kinfolk will live in the wilderness or as the garous eyes and ears in the city</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> In the wilderness: not so many. Kinfolk are normal-ish people after all. It is much more likely for them to be living in rural towns. For the actual wilderness, Garou have much better eyes and ears than kinfolk in general. Spirits are much better for that.<br /> As for cities, the only tribes to really have kinfolk in numbers there are going to be the Bone Gnawers and Glasswalkers. I think the other tribes (Silverfangs and Shadowlords especially) will sometimes have kinfolk in capital cities in positions of influence, but otherwise there isn't much for Garou there. Out is rural areas, most townships can (or at least have been able to) get away with enforcing the laws their own ways with little oversight. So using that as a base, as long as the local small town-ish authorities are kinfolk, the Garou are generally covered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T01:17:19-07:00","id":997044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cannot see Homids supporting bringing back the Impergium. It doesn't make any sense.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div> Then by that logic, the Impergium itself makes no sense to you -- since the dude who actually started it (King Rests-The-Moon) <i>was a homid</i>.<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talons can support the idea, because it doesn't affect their families at all.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div> And homids can support the idea too because...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=996890#post996890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all seriousness, most modern Garou are homid; the vast majority of most tribes have dwindling numbers of lupus. Which means that by extension, most werewolves have human mothers or fathers, and human siblings. They will very likely have human children...</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They most certainly <i>do</i> <i>not</i>. The Garou (ironically with the sole exception of the Red Talons) view their homid Kinfolk as being distinct from humanity at large. During the Impergium, they were (in the most egregious example of Garou hypocrisy ever) made exempt from the culling.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Garou, like it or not, have changed since prehistory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again... Tell that to the Bunyip.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T02:00:54-07:00","id":997054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=994813#post994813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh, yeah... because the Garou have <i>totally</i> changed. The last time they pulled that kind of garbage was the War of Tears and that was waaaaaaay back -- in the 1930s. Y'know, within living memory.</div> </div> </div> </div>The last time humans pulled that garbage was... is right now. And every day since the dawn of speech, probably.<br /> <br /> So, one can't really have the moral highground as a human towards the garou, which is kind of the point of the whole WoD. By being the Monster playing though themes totally human.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:45:02-07:00","id":997280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=997044#post997044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Then by that logic, the Impergium itself makes no sense to you -- since the dude who actually started it (King Rests-The-Moon) <i>was a homid</i>.<br /> \u200b And homids can support the idea too because...</div> </div> </div> </div>Because of politics, as the above example shows. Most of the Garou were not born of humans when the Impergium started. Now, it pulls a different way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No. They most certainly <i>do</i> <i>not</i>. The Garou (ironically with the sole exception of the Red Talons) view their homid Kinfolk as being distinct from humanity at large. During the Impergium, they were (in the most egregious example of Garou hypocrisy ever) made exempt from the culling. </div> </div> </div>The Impergium was longer ago than anything recorded in human history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again... Tell that to the Bunyip. </div> </div> </div>That was before the biggest fire under the Garou's collective asses in the modern world (WW2 in aggregate) was ignited. There's nothing like the concept of MAD to make you rethink everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T19:15:36-07:00","id":997501,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one who thinks the entry for Silencers would benefit from some degree of crunch, like a penalty to either damage and or accuracy, and what bystanders roll to hear the shot?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T00:52:42-07:00","id":997595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=997501#post997501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one who thinks the entry for Silencers would benefit from some degree of crunch, like a penalty to either damage and or accuracy, and what bystanders roll to hear the shot?</div> </div> </div> </div>Real-world silencers/suppressors don't make that much of a difference. I