ack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T20:21:36-07:00","id":998045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=997595#post997595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Real-world silencers/suppressors don't make that much of a difference. It isn't like the movies. <img src=\"http://3.bp.blogspot.com/-0fA2TBLPTfY/TV1qmwA0qlI/AAAAAAAAADU/xRD4eKTwl68/s1600/Decibel+Reference.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Oy vey ist mir that is big. Whatever. You get the idea. Given that both a regular and a 'silenced' gunshot are both louder than your average panic at the disco, I am ok with the rules being adjudicated on a case-by-case basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>The exception to that would be subsonic ammunition, which would be much quieter, around 70 db, than conventional firearms (though the damage would be reduced by a minimum of 2 dice).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:12:02-07:00","id":998365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf?p=998045#post998045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The exception to that would be subsonic ammunition, which would be much quieter, around 70 db, than conventional firearms (though the damage would be reduced by a minimum of 2 dice).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also, subsonic ammo has a tendency to jam a lot more, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12579-lordcrimson","name":"LordCrimson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T18:16:20-07:00","id":998534,"title":"","content":"Yes, but WoD does not really take that into account.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[